{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_mw4kwulxhwofdiuxbal6b3jsmeevmjpsz5efgsczaysbv4ruyq5q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_016HQkuVYD96wCMukzNpp6Ei","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write t_rowops.rs differential tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are writing ONE Rust integration-test file for a C→Rust differential verification of **libpng**.\n\nRepo root: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-SS8HRb`\n- `c_src/` — original C (READ ONLY, never modify). Already built: `c_src/build/libpng.so`.\n- `translation/` — the Rust crate (cdylib at `translation/target/release/liblibpng.so`). **You may ONLY create/modify `translation/tests/t_rowops.rs`.** Do NOT touch `translation/src/**`, `translation/tests/common/**`, `c_src/**`, `Cargo.toml`, or any other test file.\n\n## Existing harness you MUST use (read `translation/tests/common/mod.rs` and `translation/tests/common/api.rs` first)\n\n`mod common;` gives you:\n- `common::libs() -> &'static Libs` with `.c` / `.rs` (`libloading::Library`).\n- `common::api::<png_fn>(lib, args...)` — `dlsym` wrappers for ~300 libpng entry points; first arg is `&libloading::Library`. If one is missing, add a LOCAL `crate::decl_api! { fn png_foo(a: T) -> R; }` block in your own file — do NOT edit `tests/common/api.rs`.\n- `common::api::new_writer(lib)` / `new_reader(lib)` — create a `png_structp` with recording error/warning handlers and the harness I/O callbacks installed.\n- `common::capture(|| ...) -> Run<T>` catches the `png_error` unwind; `Run { out: Option<T>, log: Vec<Msg> }`, `Msg::Err(Vec<u8>)`/`Msg::Warn(Vec<u8>)`, `Run::assert_eq(&other, \"label\")`.\n- `common::Rng::new(seed)`: `.u32() .u8() .below(n) .range_i32(lo,hi) .bytes(n)`.\n- All libpng structs/constants: `png_row_info { width: u32, rowbytes: usize, color_type: u8, bit_depth: u8, channels: u8, pixel_depth: u8 }`, `png_color`, `png_color_8`, `PNG_COLOR_TYPE_*`, `PNG_FILTER_VALUE_*`, etc.\n- See `translation/tests/smoke.rs` for a working example.\n\n## Your task: create `translation/tests/t_rowops.rs`\n\nThese are the LOW-LEVEL exported row operations. One `#[test]` per row below. Every test calls BOTH `.so`s with identical inputs and asserts the mutated row buffers, the mutated `png_row_info`, and the message log are byte-identical. Use MANY randomized inputs (fixed seed per test) — hundreds of iterations, several widths, all listed variants.\n\nImportant: allocate a generously oversized row buffer (e.g. `rowbytes + 64` bytes, filled with a random-but-identical pattern) so that any over-write past `rowbytes` also shows up in the comparison. Compare the WHOLE buffer.\n\nRows (from `translation/CONFIGS.md`, numbers kept):\n19. `png_do_bgr(ri, row)`, `png_do_invert(ri, row)`, `png_do_swap(ri, row)`, `png_do_packswap(ri, row)`: color_type ∈ {0,2,3,4,6} × bit_depth ∈ {1,2,4,8,16} × width ∈ {1,2,3,7,8,9,33} × 20 random row contents each. Compute `channels` and `pixel_depth` and `rowbytes` the way libpng does (`channels` = 1 for GRAY/PALETTE, 2 for GRAY_ALPHA, 3 for RGB, 4 for RGBA; `pixel_depth = bit_depth*channels`; `rowbytes = (width * pixel_depth + 7) >> 3`). Include the combinations libpng itself would never produce (e.g. bit_depth 1 with color_type 6) — the C functions just check their own guards, so both must behave the same.\n20. `png_do_strip_channel(ri, row, at_start)`: channels ∈ {2,3,4} (color types 4, 2, 6) × bit_depth ∈ {8,16} × at_start ∈ {0,1} × widths as above. Also channels==1 (must be a no-op / same behaviour).\n21. `png_do_check_palette_indexes(pp, ri)`: needs a `png_structp` with `num_palette` and `num_palette_max` set — set those through the public API: create a WRITER, `png_create_info_struct`, `png_set_IHDR(w,h,bd,PNG_COLOR_TYPE_PALETTE,...)`, `png_set_PLTE(pp, ip, palette, num_palette)`, then `png_write_info(pp, ip)` so `png_ptr->num_palette` is set, then call `png_do_check_palette_indexes` with rows containing in-range and out-of-range indexes. num_palette ∈ {1,2,16,256} × bit_depth ∈ {1,2,4,8}. Wrap in `capture` and compare the warning log (the C emits `png_warning` / `png_app_error`-style messages here — check `c_src/src/pngtrans.c`).\n22. `png_read_filter_row(pp, ri, row, prev_row, filter)`: filter ∈ {0,1,2,3,4} plus out-of-range 5 and -1 × `pixel_depth` ∈ {1,2,4,8,16,24,32,48,64} × 30 random (row, prev_row) pairs each × widths giving rowbytes 1..40. Needs a `png_structp` (used only for `pp->rowbytes`/`transformations`? check `c_src/src/pngrutil.c`) — a `new_reader` is enough. Compare the filtered row bytes exactly.\n23. `png_do_read_interlace(ri, row, pass, transformations)`: pass ∈ 0..=6 × color_type ∈ {0,2,3,4,6} × bit_depth ∈ {1,2,4,8,16} × transformations ∈ {0, PNG_PACKSWAP} (find `PNG_PACKSWAP`'s value in `c_src/include/pngpriv.h`) × widths 1..=33. IMPORTANT: this function EXPANDS the row in place, so the buffer must be big enough for the output row (`PNG_ROWBYTES(pixel_depth, final_width)` + 64); use the same over-sized buffer for both libraries and compare all of it.\n24. `png_do_write_interlace(ri, row, pass)`: pass ∈ 0..=5 (and 6, which the C treats as a no-op) × same shapes as row 23.\n25. `png_combine_row(pp, dp, display)`: this reads `pp->row_buf`, `pp->pass`, `pp->width`, `pp->interlaced`, `pp->transformations`, `pp->row_info` — driving it standalone requires internal state you cannot set through the public API. Therefore test it INDIRECTLY but still directly-called: drive a real interlaced read (see below) and additionally call the exported `png_progressive_combine_row(pp, old_row, new_row)` (which is a thin public wrapper over `png_combine_row`) from inside the progressive row callback for a 7-pass Adam7 image, comparing the combined destination buffer after every callback. If you find a way to set the needed state through public setters, prefer the direct call. Document what you did in a comment.\n   To build the test PNGs for this row: create a writer, `png_set_IHDR(..., PNG_INTERLACE_ADAM7, ...)`, write random rows, capture the bytes with the harness sink (`common::sink_reset()`, then after writing `common::sink_take()`), then feed those bytes to a progressive reader (`png_set_progressive_read_fn` + `png_process_data`) — do the whole thing once per library and compare the final combined image bytes plus the sequence of `(row_number, pass)` callback arguments.\n\n## Rules\n- Never call the Rust crate directly — everything goes through `libs().rs` + `dlsym`.\n- Wrap anything that can `png_error` in `common::capture`.\n- The C is ALWAYS correct. If the two diverge, that is a Rust bug: **leave the test failing, do NOT fix `src/`, do NOT weaken/`#[ignore]` the assertion.** Report it precisely.\n- Build/run from `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-SS8HRb/translation`:\n  `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test t_rowops 2>&1 | tail -40`\n  (`--offline` mandatory: no network. `--release` mandatory: debug enables overflow checks the C lacks.)\n- Iterate until your file compiles cleanly.\n\n## Report back\n1. Row numbers covered → `#[test]` names.\n2. Every FAILING test with the exact divergence (inputs incl. row_info fields, C bytes vs Rust bytes as hex, message logs).\n3. Anything you could not test and why."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6388,"cache_read_input_tokens":138104,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6388,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"814b2895-9042-4f5f-bd73-35bea46615cb","uuid":"8b4d8318-f52f-43bc-b69d-0519a917a82b","timestamp":"2026-09-08T15:19:52.160Z"}
