/target/release/liblibpng.so`). **You may ONLY create/modify `translation/tests/t_write.rs`.** Do NOT touch `translation/src/**`, `translation/tests/common/**`, `c_src/**`, `Cargo.toml`, or any other test file.\n\n## Existing harness you MUST use (read `translation/tests/common/mod.rs` and `translation/tests/common/api.rs` first)\n\n`mod common;` gives you:\n- `common::libs()` → `.c` / `.rs` (`libloading::Library`).\n- `common::api::<png_fn>(lib, args...)` — `dlsym` wrappers for ~300 libpng entry points; first arg is `&libloading::Library`. Missing one? add a LOCAL `crate::decl_api! { fn png_foo(a: T) -> R; }` block in your own file — do NOT edit `tests/common/api.rs`.\n- `common::api::new_writer(lib)` — `png_create_write_struct` with the recording error/warning handlers AND `png_set_write_fn(pp, ptr, write_cb, flush_cb)` already installed. All bytes libpng writes go to a thread-local sink:\n  - `common::sink_reset()` before you start,\n  - `common::sink_take() -> (Vec<u8>, usize /*flush count*/)` afterwards.\n- `common::capture(|| ...) -> Run<T>` catches the `png_error` unwind (the error handler records the message then panics — the stand-in for the app's `longjmp`). `Run { out: Option<T>, log: Vec<Msg> }`, `Msg::Err(Vec<u8>)`/`Msg::Warn(Vec<u8>)`, `Run::assert_eq(&other, \"label\")`.\n- `common::Rng::new(seed)`: `.u32() .u8() .below(n) .range_i32(lo,hi) .bytes(n)`.\n- All libpng structs/constants are in `common` (`png_color`, `png_color_8`, `png_color_16`, `png_time`, `png_text`, `png_sPLT_t`, `png_sPLT_entry`, `png_unknown_chunk`, `PNG_COLOR_TYPE_*`, `PNG_FILTER_*`, `PNG_TRANSFORM_*`, `PNG_INTERLACE_*`, `PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_*`, `PNG_HAVE_IHDR`/`PNG_HAVE_PLTE`/`PNG_AFTER_IDAT`, …).\n- `translation/tests/smoke.rs` is a working example.\n\n## Your task: create `translation/tests/t_write.rs` — the WRITE side\n\nCentral pattern (write once per library, compare the produced PNG byte streams):\n```rust\nfn write_with<F: Fn(&Library, png_structp, png_infop)>(setup: F) -> common::Run<(Vec<u8>, usize)> { /* per library */ }\n```\nFor each configuration: `sink_reset()`, `new_writer(lib)`, `png_create_info_struct`, apply the configuration, `png_write_info`, write the rows, `png_write_end`, `png_destroy_write_struct`, then `sink_take()`. Wrap the whole thing in `common::capture`. Do this for `libs().c` and `libs().rs` and assert the byte vectors, the flush count and the message log are IDENTICAL. Report the first differing byte offset in the assert message.\n\nRows to cover (from `translation/CONFIGS.md`; keep the numbers in test names, e.g. `fn cfg28_chunk_writers()`):\n\n28. **Low-level chunk writers called directly** (NOT via png_write_info): `png_write_sig`, `png_write_IHDR`, `png_write_PLTE`, `png_write_IEND`, `png_write_gAMA_fixed`, `png_write_sRGB`, `png_write_sBIT` (all 5 colour types), `png_write_cHRM_fixed` (takes a `*const png_xy`; look up `png_xy` field order in `c_src/include/pngpriv.h` and define it `#[repr(C)]` locally), `png_write_cICP`, `png_write_cLLI_fixed`, `png_write_mDCV_fixed`, `png_write_tRNS`, `png_write_bKGD`, `png_write_hIST`, `png_write_oFFs`, `png_write_pHYs`, `png_write_tIME`, `png_write_eXIf`, `png_write_tEXt`, `png_write_zTXt`, `png_write_iTXt`, `png_write_sCAL_s`, `png_write_pCAL` (all 5 equation types, 0..3 params), `png_write_iCCP`, `png_write_sPLT`, `png_write_chunk`, `png_write_chunk_start`+`png_write_chunk_data`+`png_write_chunk_end`. Use several valid value sets each (randomised where sensible) and compare the exact emitted bytes.\n29. `png_write_png` one-shot: every valid (color_type, bit_depth) pair — GRAY 1/2/4/8/16, RGB 8/16, PALETTE 1/2/4/8, GRAY_ALPHA 8/16, RGBA 8/16 — × interlace ∈ {0,1} × sizes (w,h) ∈ {(1,1),(7,3),(8,8),(9,17),(33,5)} × `transforms` ∈ {IDENTITY, PACKING, PACKSWAP, INVERT_MONO, SHIFT, BGR, SWAP_ALPHA, SWAP_ENDIAN, INVERT_ALPHA, STRIP_FILLER_BEFORE, STRIP_FILLER_AFTER}. Rows are random bytes from a fixed seed. Note `png_write_png` needs `png_set_rows` (or an `info_ptr` with rows) — set rows with `png_set_rows(pp, ip, rows_ptr_array)`. Prune combinations the C rejects, but if you are unsure just run it inside `capture` and compare the error too.\n30. The same shapes driven through the LOW-LEVEL pipeline: `png_write_info` + `png_write_row` per row / `png_write_rows` / `png_write_image` + `png_write_end`. Verify all three row-writing entry points give identical output in both libraries.\n31. `png_set_filter(pp, PNG_FILTER_TYPE_BASE, mask)` with mask ∈ {PNG_NO_FILTERS, PNG_FILTER_NONE, PNG_FILTER_SUB, PNG_FILTER_UP, PNG_FILTER_AVG, PNG_FILTER_PAETH, PNG_ALL_FILTERS, PNG_FILTER_SUB|PNG_FILTER_PAETH} × a few (color_type, bit_depth) × interlace ∈ {0,1}.\n32. `png_set_compression_level` ∈ {-1,0,1,6,9} × `png_set_compression_strategy` ∈ {0,1,2,3,4} × `png_set_compression_window_bits` ∈ {8,9,15} × `png_set_compression_mem_level` ∈ {1,8,9} (sample the cross product, at least 60 combinations) on an 8-bit RGB image big enough to compress (e.g. 64×64).\n33. `png_set_compression_buffer_size` ∈ {1,2,3,1024,8192,65536} — forces multi-IDAT splitting; also compare `png_get_compression_buffer_size`.\n34. `png_set_flush(pp, rows)` with rows ∈ {0,1,2,height} plus an explicit `png_write_flush` mid-image: compare the byte stream AND the flush count from `sink_take()`.\n35. Text chunks: `png_set_text` with tEXt (compression -1), zTXt (0), iTXt none (1), iTXt deflate (2); key lengths 1 and 79; text = empty, 1 byte, 10 kB of random bytes; also the `png_set_text_compression_level/mem_level/strategy/window_bits/method` variants.\n36. All ancillary chunks set via `png_set_*` before `png_write_info`, singly and then all together: gAMA(+fixed), cHRM(+fixed, +XYZ_fixed), sRGB, sRGB_gAMA_and_cHRM, iCCP, sBIT, bKGD, hIST, tRNS, oFFs, pHYs, sCAL (double, fixed and string forms), pCAL (all 5 equation types, 0..N params), tIME, eXIf_1, sPLT, mDCV_fixed, cLLI_fixed, cICP.\n37. `png_set_unknown_chunks(pp, ip, chunks, n)` + `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks(pp, keep, list, n)`: location ∈ {PNG_HAVE_IHDR, PNG_HAVE_PLTE, PNG_AFTER_IDAT} × keep ∈ {DEFAULT, NEVER, IF_SAFE, ALWAYS} × safe (lower-case 2nd letter, e.g. `b\"nEwC\"`… check the PNG safe-to-copy rules) and unsafe chunk names × 0/1/3 chunks. Also `png_set_unknown_chunk_location` and `png_handle_as_unknown`.\n\n## Rules\n- Never call the Rust crate directly — everything through `dlsym` on both `.so`s.\n- Wrap everything that can `png_error` in `common::capture`; create a fresh png_struct per capture.\n- **Any C↔Rust divergence is a Rust bug. Leave the test failing; do NOT modify `src/`, do NOT weaken or `#[ignore]` an assertion.** Report the divergence precisely.\n- Keep the total runtime of the file under ~4 minutes: prune the cross-products with a fixed-seed random sample instead of running everything.\n- Build/run from `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-SS8HRb/translation`:\n  `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test t_write 2>&1 | tail -60`\n  (`--offline` mandatory: no network. `--release` mandatory: the debug profile enables overflow checks the C does not have.)\n- Iterate until the file compiles cleanly.\n\n## Report back\n1. Row numbers covered → `#[test]` names.\n2. Every FAILING test with the exact divergence: the configuration, the first differing byte offset, ~16 bytes of C vs Rust output around it (hex), and both message logs.\n3. Anything you could not test and why.","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-6wP1XG/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-SS8HRb/814b2895-9042-4f5f-bd73-35bea46615cb/tasks/a5c6a9b43ac59710d.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
