{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_t55fmb2k2ejv35efpoy667jyuv34oja4pd6bsrvwmqiqsm4bxzpa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01Y3QfJuZCTs1j1jAHPmPmNv","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write t_read.rs differential tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are writing ONE Rust integration-test file for a C→Rust differential verification of **libpng**.\n\nRepo root: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-SS8HRb`\n- `c_src/` — original C (READ ONLY, never modify). Already built: `c_src/build/libpng.so`.\n- `translation/` — the Rust crate (cdylib at `translation/target/release/liblibpng.so`). **You may ONLY create/modify `translation/tests/t_read.rs`.** Do NOT touch `translation/src/**`, `translation/tests/common/**`, `c_src/**`, `Cargo.toml`, or any other test file.\n\n## Existing harness you MUST use (read `translation/tests/common/mod.rs` and `translation/tests/common/api.rs` first)\n\n`mod common;` gives you:\n- `common::libs()` → `.c` / `.rs` (`libloading::Library`).\n- `common::api::<png_fn>(lib, args...)` — `dlsym` wrappers for ~300 libpng entry points; first arg is `&libloading::Library`. Missing one? add a LOCAL `crate::decl_api! { fn png_foo(a: T) -> R; }` block in your own file — do NOT edit `tests/common/api.rs`.\n- `common::api::new_writer(lib)` — writer whose output goes to a thread-local sink: `common::sink_reset()`, then `common::sink_take() -> (Vec<u8>, usize)`.\n- `common::api::new_reader(lib)` — reader whose input comes from a thread-local source: call `common::src_set(&png_bytes)` first; `common::src_pos()` tells how much was consumed.\n- `common::capture(|| ...) -> Run<T>` catches the `png_error` unwind (the error handler records the message then panics — the stand-in for the app's `longjmp`). `Run { out: Option<T>, log: Vec<Msg> }`, `Msg::Err(Vec<u8>)`/`Msg::Warn(Vec<u8>)`, `Run::assert_eq(&other, \"label\")`.\n- `common::Rng::new(seed)`: `.u32() .u8() .below(n) .range_i32(lo,hi) .bytes(n)`.\n- All libpng structs/constants are in `common`.\n- `translation/tests/smoke.rs` is a working example.\n\n## Your task: create `translation/tests/t_read.rs` — the READ side\n\nYou need PNG test inputs. Generate them ONCE with the **C** library (it is ground truth) using `new_writer` + `png_set_IHDR` + random rows + `png_write_info`/`png_write_image`/`png_write_end`, and cache them (e.g. a `fn make_png(color_type, bit_depth, interlace, w, h, seed) -> Vec<u8>` helper). Then decode each with BOTH libraries and compare.\n\nCentral pattern: `src_set(&png)`, `new_reader(lib)`, `png_create_info_struct`, apply options, `png_read_info`, read the IHDR back through every relevant `png_get_*`, `png_read_update_info`, allocate rows of `png_get_rowbytes()`, `png_read_image`/`png_read_row`, `png_read_end`, `png_destroy_read_struct`. Collect a comparison tuple of (all getters, all decoded row bytes, message log, `src_pos()`) and assert C == Rust. Wrap in `common::capture`.\n\nRows to cover (numbers from `translation/CONFIGS.md`; name tests `cfg38_...` etc.):\n\n38. Round-trip decode with NO transforms: every valid (color_type, bit_depth) — GRAY 1/2/4/8/16, RGB 8/16, PALETTE 1/2/4/8, GRAY_ALPHA 8/16, RGBA 8/16 — × interlace ∈ {0,1} × (w,h) ∈ {(1,1),(7,3),(8,8),(9,17),(33,5)}. Exercise all three read entry points: `png_read_image`, per-row `png_read_row(row, NULL)` and `png_read_row(NULL, display_row)`, `png_read_rows`, plus the one-shot `png_read_png` with `PNG_TRANSFORM_IDENTITY`.\n39. One test per READ TRANSFORM, each on an input where it applies: `png_set_palette_to_rgb`, `png_set_tRNS_to_alpha`, `png_set_expand`, `png_set_expand_gray_1_2_4_to_8`, `png_set_expand_16`, `png_set_gray_to_rgb`, `png_set_rgb_to_gray_fixed` (error_action 1/2/3 × default coefficients (-1,-1) and custom), `png_set_background_fixed` (bg_gamma_code ∈ {SCREEN, FILE, UNIQUE} × need_expand ∈ {0,1}), `png_set_alpha_mode_fixed` (mode ∈ {PNG_ALPHA_PNG, PNG_ALPHA_STANDARD, PNG_ALPHA_OPTIMIZED, PNG_ALPHA_BROKEN} × gamma ∈ {PNG_FP_1, 220000, PNG_DEFAULT_sRGB}), `png_set_gamma_fixed` (screen/file ∈ {100000, 45455, 220000}), `png_set_quantize` (max_colors ∈ {2,16,255}, with and without a histogram, full_quantize 0/1), `png_set_strip_16`, `png_set_scale_16`, `png_set_packing`, `png_set_packswap`, `png_set_swap`, `png_set_swap_alpha`, `png_set_invert_mono`, `png_set_invert_alpha`, `png_set_filler` (PNG_FILLER_BEFORE/AFTER), `png_set_add_alpha` (both), `png_set_shift`, `png_set_strip_alpha`, `png_set_bgr`, `png_set_interlace_handling` (compare its return value too), and `png_set_read_user_transform_fn` + `png_set_user_transform_info` (the callback must record the `png_row_info` it is handed and mutate the row deterministically; compare the recorded sequence).\n40. Transform COMBINATIONS (each its own assertion): expand+gray_to_rgb+add_alpha+swap; background+gamma+strip_16; palette_to_rgb+expand_16+bgr; expand then quantize; rgb_to_gray+background+alpha_mode; strip_alpha+packing+packswap+invert_mono.\n41. `png_read_update_info` called 0×, 1×, 2× before reading rows, and `png_start_read_image`; after each, compare `png_get_rowbytes`, `png_get_channels`, `png_get_bit_depth`, `png_get_color_type`, `png_get_interlace_type`, and the message log (calling it twice emits a warning in the C — check `c_src/src/pngread.c`).\n42. Progressive read: `png_set_progressive_read_fn(pp, ptr, info_cb, row_cb, end_cb)` + `png_process_data` with feed granularity ∈ {1,2,3,7,13,whole buffer} × interlace ∈ {0,1} × all colour types. The callbacks must record everything (all row bytes, `(row_num, pass)` pairs, the info-callback getters) into a thread-local; compare the whole recording between the two libraries. Also compare `png_get_progressive_ptr`.\n43. `png_process_data_pause(pp, save)` with save ∈ {0,1} from inside the row callback, and `png_process_data_skip` — compare the returned byte counts and the eventual decoded image.\n44. `png_progressive_combine_row` for an interlaced image, all 7 passes: maintain a display buffer per row and compare it after every callback.\n45. `png_set_crc_action(crit, ancil)`: crit ∈ {PNG_CRC_DEFAULT, PNG_CRC_ERROR_QUIT, PNG_CRC_WARN_USE, PNG_CRC_QUIET_USE, PNG_CRC_NO_CHANGE} × ancil ∈ the same set, on (a) a stream with a corrupted IDAT CRC and (b) a stream with a corrupted ancillary (e.g. tEXt) CRC. Compare error/warning logs and whatever decodes.\n46. `png_set_benign_errors(0)` vs `(1)` on a stream with a truncated/corrupt ancillary chunk.\n47. `png_set_user_limits(w,h)`, `png_set_chunk_cache_max(n)`, `png_set_chunk_malloc_max(n)` with values above / exactly at / below the actual image width, height, chunk count and chunk size; also compare `png_get_user_width_max`, `png_get_user_height_max`, `png_get_chunk_cache_max`, `png_get_chunk_malloc_max`.\n48. `png_set_read_user_chunk_fn` with a callback returning -1, 0 and +1 on a private chunk you injected into the stream; compare the callback invocation record and `png_get_user_chunk_ptr`.\n49. `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks` handling ∈ {DEFAULT, NEVER, IF_SAFE, ALWAYS} × global (num=0) vs a per-chunk list; compare `png_get_unknown_chunks` output (name, size, location, data) and `png_handle_as_unknown` / `png_chunk_unknown_handling`.\n50. `png_set_option(option, onoff)` for `PNG_MAXIMUM_INFLATE_WINDOW`, `PNG_SKIP_sRGB_CHECK_PROFILE`, `PNG_IGNORE_ADLER32` × {PNG_OPTION_OFF, PNG_OPTION_ON} — compare the return value and the decode result.\n51. `png_permit_mng_features(0)` and `(PNG_ALL_MNG_FEATURES)` — compare the return value; if you can construct a filter-method-64 stream, decode it too.\n54. Every `png_get_*` accessor after `png_read_info` on a stream that contains every chunk type (build it with the C writer, setting gAMA, cHRM, sRGB, iCCP, sBIT, bKGD, hIST, tRNS, oFFs, pHYs, sCAL, pCAL, tIME, eXIf, sPLT, text, unknown chunks): compare EVERY out-parameter, including `png_get_pHYs_dpi`, `png_get_pixels_per_inch`, `png_get_x_offset_inches