{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"ac0af778c6d0e82df","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01LbBxjEteijbrPPa5EWUuMx","description":"Write t_simple.rs differential tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","is_backgrounded":true,"spawn_depth":1,"task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are writing ONE Rust integration-test file for a C→Rust differential verification of **libpng**.\n\nRepo root: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-SS8HRb`\n- `c_src/` — original C (READ ONLY, never modify). Already built: `c_src/build/libpng.so`.\n- `translation/` — the Rust crate (cdylib at `translation/target/release/liblibpng.so`). **You may ONLY create/modify `translation/tests/t_simple.rs`.** Do NOT touch `translation/src/**`, `translation/tests/common/**`, `c_src/**`, `Cargo.toml`, or any other test file.\n\n## Existing harness you MUST use (read `translation/tests/common/mod.rs` and `translation/tests/common/api.rs` first)\n\n`mod common;` gives you:\n- `common::libs()` → `.c` / `.rs` (`libloading::Library`).\n- `common::api::<png_fn>(lib, args...)` — `dlsym` wrappers, first arg `&libloading::Library`. Missing one? add a LOCAL `crate::decl_api! { fn png_foo(a: T) -> R; }` block in your own file — do NOT edit `tests/common/api.rs`.\n- `png_image` is already defined in `common` as `#[repr(C)] { opaque: *mut c_void, version: u32, width: u32, height: u32, format: u32, flags: u32, colormap_entries: u32, warning_or_error: u32, message: [c_char; 64] }` with `Default` (version=1), `.msg() -> String` and `.cmp_key()` (everything except `opaque`).\n- Wrappers already present: `png_image_begin_read_from_memory`, `png_image_begin_read_from_file`, `png_image_begin_read_from_stdio`, `png_image_finish_read`, `png_image_free`, `png_image_write_to_memory`, `png_image_write_to_file`, `png_image_write_to_stdio`.\n- All `PNG_FORMAT_*` / `PNG_FORMAT_FLAG_*` / `PNG_IMAGE_VERSION` constants are in `common`.\n- `common::capture(|| ...) -> Run<T>` catches an error unwind; `Run::assert_eq(&other, \"label\")`.\n- `common::Rng::new(seed)`: `.u32() .u8() .below(n) .bytes(n)`.\n- `common::api::new_writer(lib)` + `common::sink_reset()` / `sink_take()` if you need to build PNG inputs with the low-level API.\n- `translation/tests/smoke.rs` is a working example.\n\nUseful C macros you will need to reimplement in Rust (read them in `c_src/include/png.h`, search for `PNG_IMAGE_ROW_STRIDE`, `PNG_IMAGE_SIZE`, `PNG_IMAGE_COLORMAP_SIZE`, `PNG_IMAGE_SAMPLE_CHANNELS`, `PNG_IMAGE_PIXEL_CHANNELS`, `PNG_IMAGE_SAMPLE_COMPONENT_SIZE`, `PNG_IMAGE_BUFFER_SIZE`) — port them exactly as small Rust `fn`s.\n\n## Your task: create `translation/tests/t_simple.rs` — the SIMPLIFIED API\n\nRows (numbers from `translation/CONFIGS.md`; name tests `cfg59_...` etc.):\n\n59. **Simplified read from memory.** Build a set of PNG inputs with the C low-level writer (every valid colour type / bit depth, interlaced and not, a few sizes incl. 1×1 and 33×5) — or, simpler, produce them with `png_image_write_to_memory` from the C library. For each input, decode with `png_image_begin_read_from_memory` then `png_image_finish_read` for output `format` ∈ the full meaningful cross-product of {GRAY, GA, AG, RGB, BGR, RGBA, ARGB, BGRA, ABGR} × {8-bit, LINEAR} × {direct, COLORMAP} × `row_stride` ∈ {natural positive, natural negative (bottom-up)} × `background` ∈ {NULL, a set png_color}. Compare, between C and Rust: the return values of BOTH calls, `image.cmp_key()` after each call (width/height/format/flags/colormap_entries/warning_or_error/message), the ENTIRE output buffer bytes, and the colormap bytes when a colormap format is used. Allocate the buffer with `PNG_IMAGE_SIZE`-equivalent and pre-fill it with a fixed non-zero pattern so that untouched bytes are also compared.\n60. Simplified read from file and from stdio: write one of the PNG inputs to a temp file (use `std::env::temp_dir()`; the sandbox-writable temp dir is in the `TMPDIR` env var — prefer `std::env::temp_dir()`), then `png_image_begin_read_from_file` and (with `libc`-free plain FFI: get `fopen`/`fclose` by `dlsym`-ing them out of the already-loaded process with `libloading::os::unix::Library::this()`, or simply declare `extern \"C\" { fn fopen(p: *const c_char, m: *const c_char) -> *mut c_void; fn fclose(f: *mut c_void) -> c_int; }`) `png_image_begin_read_from_stdio`. Same comparisons as row 59 for a handful of formats.\n61. **Simplified write to memory.** For each in-memory image shape (format cross-product as in row 59, sizes 1×1, 7×3, 32×32; random pixel data from a fixed seed; colormap formats with a random 256-entry colormap) call `png_image_write_to_memory` (a) with `memory == NULL` to query the size, then (b) with a buffer of exactly that size, then (c) with a buffer one byte too small. Compare return values, `*memory_bytes`, the produced PNG bytes and `image.cmp_key()`. Also `convert_to_8bit` ∈ {0,1} and `row_stride` positive and negative.\n62. Simplified write to file and to stdio — byte-compare the two resulting files.\n63. `png_image_free` after a successful read, after a failed read, and on an all-zero `png_image`; `png_image_error`-driven paths (both libraries must leave `warning_or_error` and `message` identical). Also verify calling `png_image_finish_read` twice, and `png_image_free` twice, behave identically.\n\n## Rules\n- Never call the Rust crate directly — everything through `dlsym` on both `.so`s.\n- Wrap calls in `common::capture` (the simplified API normally returns 0 instead of longjmping, but be safe).\n- **Any C↔Rust divergence is a Rust bug. Leave the test failing; do NOT modify `src/`, do NOT weaken or `#[ignore]` an assertion.** Report the divergence precisely.\n- Keep runtime under ~4 minutes; prune with fixed-seed sampling.\n- Build/run from `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-SS8HRb/translation`:\n  `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test t_simple 2>&1 | tail -60`\n  (`--offline` mandatory: no network. `--release` mandatory: the debug profile enables overflow checks the C does not have.)\n- Iterate until the file compiles cleanly.\n\n## Report back\n1. Row numbers covered → `#[test]` names.\n2. Every FAILING test with the exact divergence: configuration, first differing byte offset, ~16 bytes of C vs Rust around it (hex), the two `png_image` states and messages.\n3. Anything you could not test and why.","uuid":"40d3764e-a8e7-4ba6-8926-5a1e32b81d0c","session_id":"814b2895-9042-4f5f-bd73-35bea46615cb"}
