{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a11472bbc60484d02","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Vd7RCgzqQMCnW9rPtUEPZ6","description":"Write t_mem.rs differential tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","is_backgrounded":true,"spawn_depth":1,"task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are writing ONE Rust integration-test file for a C→Rust differential verification of **libpng**.\n\nRepo root: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-SS8HRb`\n- `c_src/` — original C (READ ONLY, never modify). Already built: `c_src/build/libpng.so`.\n- `translation/` — the Rust crate (cdylib at `translation/target/release/liblibpng.so`). **You may ONLY create/modify `translation/tests/t_mem.rs`.** Do NOT touch `translation/src/**`, `translation/tests/common/**`, `c_src/**`, `Cargo.toml`, or any other test file.\n\n## Existing harness you MUST use (read `translation/tests/common/mod.rs` and `translation/tests/common/api.rs` first)\n\n`mod common;` gives you:\n- `common::libs()` → `.c` / `.rs` (`libloading::Library`).\n- `common::api::<png_fn>(lib, args...)` — `dlsym` wrappers for ~300 libpng entry points; first arg `&libloading::Library`. Missing one? add a LOCAL `crate::decl_api! { fn png_foo(a: T) -> R; }` block in your own file — do NOT edit `tests/common/api.rs`.\n- `common::api::new_writer(lib)` / `new_reader(lib)`; sink: `common::sink_reset()` / `sink_take()`; source: `common::src_set(&bytes)` / `src_pos()`.\n- `common::capture(|| ...) -> Run<T>` catches the `png_error` unwind (handler records message then panics). `Run { out: Option<T>, log: Vec<Msg> }`, `Msg::Err`/`Msg::Warn`, `Run::assert_eq(&other, \"label\")`.\n- `common::Rng::new(seed)`.\n- All libpng structs/constants.\n- `translation/tests/smoke.rs` is a working example.\n\n## Your task: create `translation/tests/t_mem.rs`\n\nRows (numbers from `translation/CONFIGS.md`; name tests `cfg52_...` etc.):\n\n52. **Custom allocator + the allocation API.** Use `png_create_read_struct_2` / `png_create_write_struct_2` and `png_set_mem_fn` with your own `malloc_fn`/`free_fn` that record (size, sequence) into a thread-local and delegate to the real `malloc`/`free` (declare them `extern \"C\" { fn malloc(n: usize) -> *mut c_void; fn free(p: *mut c_void); }`). Then drive a complete write and a complete read and compare the FULL RECORDED ALLOCATION SEQUENCE (the ordered list of requested sizes) between the C and Rust libraries — this is a strong structural check. Also differentially test `png_malloc`, `png_malloc_warn`, `png_malloc_default`, `png_calloc`, `png_free`, `png_free_default` for sizes 0, 1, 8, 4096, 1<<20 (compare NULL-ness of the result and the message log, not the pointer value), and `png_get_mem_ptr`.\n53. **info_struct lifecycle**: `png_create_info_struct`, `png_info_init_3(&mut ip, size)` (compare behaviour for `size` == the real `sizeof(png_info)` and for a wrong/smaller size — read `c_src/src/png.c` for what it does), `png_destroy_info_struct`, `png_free_data(pp, ip, mask, num)` for every `PNG_FREE_*` mask with `num` = -1 and 0..N, and `png_data_freer(pp, ip, freer, mask)` with freer ∈ {PNG_DESTROY_WILL_FREE_DATA, PNG_SET_WILL_FREE_DATA, PNG_USER_WILL_FREE_DATA}. Populate the info struct first (PLTE, tRNS, hIST, text, sPLT, iCCP, unknown chunks, pCAL, sCAL, rows) so the frees actually do work, and after each free compare `png_get_valid` for every `PNG_INFO_*` bit plus the message log. `PNG_FREE_*` values are in `c_src/include/png.h` — grep for `#define PNG_FREE_`.\n57. **ICC profile checks**: `png_icc_check_header(pp, colorspace, name, proflen, profile, color_type)`, `png_icc_check_length(...)`, `png_icc_check_tag_table(...)`. `colorspace` is a `png_colorspacerp` — find `png_colorspace` in `c_src/include/pngstruct.h` and define it `#[repr(C)]` locally (zero it before each call, and compare its FULL contents after the call as well as the return value and message log). Build a minimal valid ICC profile by hand (128-byte header + tag count + tag table; see `png_icc_check_header` in `c_src/src/png.c` for the exact required fields: size, `data_colour_space`, `profile_class`, `pcs`, `illuminant`, version, tag count, …) and then vary: profile length at the boundaries the C checks (132, 133, one below the minimum, one above `PNG_UINT_31_MAX`), tag count 0/1/many, wrong signature, wrong colour space for the given `color_type`. Also `png_resolve_file_gamma` if it takes arguments you can supply (check `pngpriv.h`).\n66. **CRC and zstream helpers**: `png_reset_crc(pp)` + `png_calculate_crc(pp, ptr, len)` over random buffers of length 0, 1, 2, 255, 4096 (chained calls too) — you cannot read the crc back directly, so verify it indirectly: after `png_reset_crc` + `png_calculate_crc`, call `png_write_chunk`-style paths, OR compare the observable behaviour of `png_reset_zstream(pp)` (compare the returned int) and `png_zalloc(pp, items, size)` / `png_zfree(pp, ptr)` (compare NULL-ness and the message log for items*size == 0 and for an overflowing product such as items=0xFFFFFFFF, size=0xFFFFFFFF). If you find no public way to observe the CRC, say so in a comment and instead verify that a written chunk's trailing 4 CRC bytes are identical between the libraries (they are, via `png_write_chunk`), which is what `png_calculate_crc` feeds.\n67. **Low-level chunk reading**: `png_read_chunk_header(pp)` (returns the chunk length and sets `pp->chunk_name`; compare the returned length and the subsequent `png_get_io_chunk_type(pp)`), then `png_handle_chunk` / `png_handle_unknown` if their signatures allow being driven directly (check `c_src/include/pngpriv.h` for the exact prototypes — `png_handle_chunk(png_structrp, png_inforp, png_uint_32 length)` and `png_handle_unknown(png_structrp, png_inforp, png_uint_32 length, int keep)`; `png_handle_unknown` returns a `png_handle_result_code` int). Drive them on a hand-built stream containing, one at a time, each known ancillary chunk plus an unknown one. Sequence: `src_set(&stream)`, `new_reader`, `png_set_sig_bytes(pp, 8)` or feed the signature via `png_read_info`, then loop `png_read_chunk_header` + `png_handle_chunk`. Compare the returned codes, the resulting `png_get_valid` bits, and the message logs. Wrap everything in `common::capture`.\n\n## Rules\n- Never call the Rust crate directly — everything through `dlsym` on both `.so`s.\n- Wrap everything that can `png_error` in `common::capture`; create a fresh png_struct per capture.\n- **Any C↔Rust divergence is a Rust bug. Leave the test failing; do NOT modify `src/`, do NOT weaken or `#[ignore]` an assertion.** Report the divergence precisely.\n- Never compare raw heap pointer VALUES between the libraries (they always differ) — compare null-ness, sizes, contents and sequences.\n- Build/run from `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-SS8HRb/translation`:\n  `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test t_mem 2>&1 | tail -60`\n  (`--offline` mandatory: no network. `--release` mandatory: the debug profile enables overflow checks the C does not have.)\n- Iterate until the file compiles cleanly.\n\n## Report back\n1. Row numbers covered → `#[test]` names.\n2. Every FAILING test with the exact divergence.\n3. Anything you could not test and why (especially where no public observation point exists).","uuid":"9cde0ba2-6a3e-4323-b8eb-97f3507df332","session_id":"814b2895-9042-4f5f-bd73-35bea46615cb"}
