{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_acxbsddad3zni557fkoo54tuaaokncsehxm7mymwi5lzpys6npoq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_012M3mdF1NGDE8vXy56KWEEg","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write t_err1.rs error-path tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are writing ONE Rust integration-test file for the **error-path** half of a C→Rust differential verification of **libpng**.\n\nRepo root: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-SS8HRb`\n- `c_src/` — original C (READ ONLY, never modify). Already built: `c_src/build/libpng.so`.\n- `translation/` — the Rust crate (cdylib at `translation/target/release/liblibpng.so`). **You may ONLY create/modify `translation/tests/t_err1.rs`.** Do NOT touch `translation/src/**`, `translation/tests/common/**`, `c_src/**`, `Cargo.toml`, or any other test file.\n\n## Existing harness you MUST use (read `translation/tests/common/mod.rs` and `translation/tests/common/api.rs` first)\n\n`mod common;` gives you:\n- `common::libs()` → `.c` / `.rs` (`libloading::Library`).\n- `common::api::<png_fn>(lib, args...)` — `dlsym` wrappers for ~300 libpng entry points; first arg `&libloading::Library`. Missing one? add a LOCAL `crate::decl_api! { fn png_foo(a: T) -> R; }` block in your own file — do NOT edit `tests/common/api.rs`.\n- `common::api::new_writer(lib)` / `new_reader(lib)` — a png_struct with `rec_error`/`rec_warning` installed. `rec_error` records the exact message bytes then panics (the stand-in for the app's `longjmp`); `rec_warning` records and returns.\n- `common::capture(|| ...) -> Run<T>` catches that unwind. `Run { out: Option<T>, log: Vec<Msg> }` with `Msg::Err(Vec<u8>)` / `Msg::Warn(Vec<u8>)`. `Run::assert_eq(&other, \"label\")` compares the message log AND the output.\n- Sink for writes: `common::sink_reset()` / `sink_take() -> (Vec<u8>, usize)`. Source for reads: `common::src_set(&bytes)` / `src_pos()`.\n- `common::Rng::new(seed)`; all libpng structs/constants.\n- `translation/tests/smoke.rs` is a working example (it triggers `png_set_sig_bytes(pp, 9)` → `png_error \"Too many bytes for PNG signature\"`).\n\n## Your task: create `translation/tests/t_err1.rs`\n\nYour assigned rejection sites are listed in **`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-SS8HRb/.verify/E1.md`** — 73 rows covering `png.c`, `pngerror.c`, `pngmem.c`, `pngget.c`, `pngtrans.c`. Each row gives the global row number (matching `translation/ERRORS.md`), the enclosing C function, file:line, the error macro, the guarding condition and the message text. **Read that file first**, then read the relevant C code around each `file:line` in `c_src/src/` to work out exactly which public API call with which arguments reaches that site.\n\nFor EACH row write a differential assertion: construct that exact invalid input/condition, call it on BOTH libraries, and assert they produce the SAME outcome — the same error/warning message bytes in the same order AND the same return value / sentinel (`Run::assert_eq`). Group related rows into one `#[test]` fn where natural, but name every test so the row numbers it covers are obvious (e.g. `err_png_c_check_ihdr_rows_7_23`), and put a `// row N` comment on each individual assertion so coverage is auditable.\n\nIf a row is genuinely UNREACHABLE from the exported API surface (all 384 C symbols are exported, including the internal `png_*` ones, so most sites ARE reachable — check `nm -D c_src/build/libpng.so`), say so explicitly in a comment naming the row number and why, and still cover everything you can.\n\n**Also cover these generic boundaries in this file** (they belong to your files' functions):\n- NULL `png_ptr` and NULL `info_ptr` passed to every `pngget.c` accessor and to `png_free_data`, `png_data_freer`, `png_set_invalid`, `png_get_valid`, `png_get_rowbytes`, `png_get_io_ptr`, `png_get_error_ptr`, `png_get_mem_ptr`, `png_get_progressive_ptr`, `png_get_user_chunk_ptr` — assert identical sentinels.\n- zero and oversized lengths: `png_malloc(pp, 0)`, `png_malloc(pp, usize::MAX)`, `png_calloc(pp, usize::MAX)`, `png_malloc_warn(pp, usize::MAX)`, `png_malloc_default`, `png_free(pp, NULL)`.\n- values one step past a documented range: `png_set_sig_bytes(pp, -1 / 0 / 8 / 9)`, `png_data_freer(pp, ip, 99, mask)` (out-of-range enum!), `png_set_shift` with all-zero and out-of-range `png_color_8`, `png_set_filler(pp, v, 99)` (out-of-range flag), `png_set_user_transform_info` with bad depths.\n- **out-of-range enum values across FFI** (C enums accept any int): pass 99 / -1 / 0x7fffffff wherever a `pngget.c`/`pngtrans.c`/`png.c` function takes an enum-like int, and assert both libraries agree.\n\n## Rules\n- Never call the Rust crate directly — everything through `dlsym` on both `.so`s.\n- Create a FRESH png_struct inside each `capture` where the operation may error (the error unwind leaves the struct unusable).\n- Never compare raw heap pointer VALUES between the libraries — compare null-ness, contents, sizes.\n- **The C is ALWAYS correct. Any C↔Rust divergence is a Rust bug: leave the test FAILING, do NOT modify `src/`, do NOT weaken or `#[ignore]` an assertion.** Report it precisely.\n- Build/run from `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-SS8HRb/translation`:\n  `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test t_err1 2>&1 | tail -60`\n  (`--offline` mandatory: no network. `--release` mandatory: the debug profile enables overflow checks the C does not have.)\n- Other agents are concurrently running cargo in the same directory; if cargo blocks on the build lock, just wait/retry.\n- Iterate until your file compiles cleanly.\n\n## Report back\n1. A list mapping EVERY row number in `E1.md` to the `#[test]` name that covers it, or to \"unreachable: <reason>\".\n2. Every FAILING test with the exact divergence (input, C result + log, Rust result + log)."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cac