exact `png_set_*` call and arguments that reach the site.\n\nFor EACH row write a differential assertion: construct that exact invalid input, call it on BOTH libraries, and assert the SAME outcome — identical message bytes in identical order AND the same return value / side effects (`Run::assert_eq`, plus `png_get_valid` afterwards where relevant). Group related rows into one `#[test]` fn where natural, name tests so the covered row numbers are obvious, and put a `// row N` comment on each assertion so coverage is auditable.\n\nThe `pngset.c` surface to attack (all with a fresh writer or reader + `png_create_info_struct`):\n- `png_set_PLTE` with num_palette < 1, > 256, > (1<<bit_depth) for each bit depth, and with a NULL palette.\n- `png_set_sCAL`, `png_set_sCAL_fixed`, `png_set_sCAL_s` with unit 0/3/99, zero/negative width or height, invalid ASCII strings (\"\", \"x\", \"1e\", \"-\", very long).\n- `png_set_pCAL` with type 0..5 and 99, nparams < 0 / mismatched, NULL purpose/units/params, an over-long purpose.\n- `png_set_iCCP` with a NULL/empty name, a 80-char name, `compression_type != 0`, proflen 0/1/131/132/`PNG_UINT_31_MAX`, and a profile whose embedded length disagrees with `proflen`.\n- `png_set_sPLT` with nentries <= 0, depth ∉ {8,16}, a NULL name, a NULL entries pointer, num_spalettes 0/negative.\n- `png_set_text` / `png_set_text_2` with a NULL key, an empty key, a key of 80+ chars, a key with leading/trailing spaces or control characters, `compression` ∈ {-3,-2,3,99}, a NULL text with non-zero length, and `num_text` <= 0.\n- `png_set_hIST` before/without a PLTE.\n- `png_set_tRNS` with num_trans out of range for the colour type, NULL trans, NULL trans_color.\n- `png_set_tIME` with month 0/13, day 0/32, hour 24, minute 60, second 61.\n- `png_set_cHRM_XYZ_fixed` / `png_set_cHRM_fixed` with degenerate/negative values.\n- `png_set_cICP` with reserved/invalid values; `png_set_cLLI_fixed` / `png_set_mDCV_fixed` with out-of-range values.\n- `png_set_eXIf` / `png_set_eXIf_1` with a too-short buffer and a bad byte-order marker.\n- `png_set_compression_buffer_size` with 0, 1, `usize::MAX`, and after writing has started.\n- `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks` with `keep` ∈ {-1, 4, 99} (out-of-range enum), num_chunks < 0, a NULL list with num > 0, and a chunk-name list whose entries are not 5 bytes each.\n- `png_set_unknown_chunks` with num_unknowns <= 0, a NULL array, a zero-size chunk, and `png_set_unknown_chunk_location` with `location` ∈ {0, 99} / a chunk index out of range.\n- `png_set_benign_errors(pp, allowed)` for allowed ∈ {0,1,2,99}.\n- `check_location` (static, reached through `png_set_unknown_chunks`).\n- `png_check_keyword` (reached through `png_set_text`).\n- `png_set_invalid` with an out-of-range mask.\n\n**Also cover the generic boundaries for these functions**: a NULL `png_ptr` and a NULL `info_ptr` for EVERY `png_set_*` above (must be a silent no-op or the same error in both), and out-of-range enum ints (99, -1, 0x7fffffff) wherever a `png_set_*` takes an enum-like int.\n\n## Rules\n- Never call the Rust crate directly — everything through `dlsym` on both `.so`s.\n- Create a FRESH png_struct + info_struct inside each `capture` where the operation may error.\n- Never compare raw heap pointer VALUES — compare null-ness, contents, sizes.\n- **The C is ALWAYS correct. Any C↔Rust divergence is a Rust bug: leave the test FAILING, do NOT modify `src/`, do NOT weaken or `#[ignore]` an assertion.** Report it precisely.\n- Build/run from `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-SS8HRb/translation`:\n  `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test t_err2 2>&1 | tail -60`\n  (`--offline` mandatory: no network. `--release` mandatory.)\n- Other agents are concurrently running cargo in the same directory; if cargo blocks on the build lock, wait/retry.\n- Iterate until your file compiles cleanly.\n\n## Report back\n1. A list mapping EVERY row number in `E2.md` to the `#[test]` name that covers it, or \"unreachable: <reason>\".\n2. Every FAILING test with the exact divergence (input, C result + log, Rust result + log).","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-6wP1XG/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-SS8HRb/814b2895-9042-4f5f-bd73-35bea46615cb/tasks/a4594d70fc141ff0b.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
