{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"aff73f574a1167c33","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01SG4CM3rdnomx5WxDKuL7GN","description":"Write t_err4.rs error-path tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","is_backgrounded":true,"spawn_depth":1,"task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are writing ONE Rust integration-test file for the **error-path** half of a C→Rust differential verification of **libpng**.\n\nRepo root: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-SS8HRb`\n- `c_src/` — original C (READ ONLY, never modify). Already built: `c_src/build/libpng.so`.\n- `translation/` — the Rust crate (cdylib at `translation/target/release/liblibpng.so`). **You may ONLY create/modify `translation/tests/t_err4.rs`.** Do NOT touch `translation/src/**`, `translation/tests/common/**`, `c_src/**`, `Cargo.toml`, or any other test file.\n\n## Existing harness you MUST use (read `translation/tests/common/mod.rs` and `translation/tests/common/api.rs` first)\n\n`mod common;` gives you:\n- `common::libs()` → `.c` / `.rs` (`libloading::Library`).\n- `common::api::<png_fn>(lib, args...)` — `dlsym` wrappers for ~300 libpng entry points; first arg `&libloading::Library`. Missing one? add a LOCAL `crate::decl_api! { fn png_foo(a: T) -> R; }` block in your own file — do NOT edit `tests/common/api.rs`.\n- `common::api::new_writer(lib)` / `new_reader(lib)` — a png_struct with `rec_error`/`rec_warning` installed. `rec_error` records the exact message bytes then panics (the stand-in for the app's `longjmp`).\n- `common::capture(|| ...) -> Run<T>` catches that unwind. `Run { out: Option<T>, log: Vec<Msg> }`, `Msg::Err(Vec<u8>)` / `Msg::Warn(Vec<u8>)`, `Run::assert_eq(&other, \"label\")`.\n- Sink for writes: `common::sink_reset()` / `sink_take()`. Source for reads: `common::src_set(&bytes)` / `src_pos()`.\n- `common::Rng::new(seed)`; all libpng structs/constants.\n- `translation/tests/smoke.rs` is a working example.\n\n## Your task: create `translation/tests/t_err4.rs`\n\nYour assigned rejection sites are listed in **`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-SS8HRb/.verify/E4.md`** — 63 rows in `c_src/src/pngrutil.c`, `pngpread.c`, `pngrio.c`, `pngwio.c`. Each row gives the global row number (matching `translation/ERRORS.md`), the enclosing C function, file:line, the error macro, the guarding condition and the message. **Read that file first**, then read the C around each `file:line`.\n\nFor EACH row write a differential assertion: construct the exact invalid input/condition, call BOTH libraries, assert the SAME outcome — identical message bytes in identical order AND the same return value/sentinel (`Run::assert_eq`). Group related rows into one `#[test]` where natural; name tests so covered row numbers are obvious; put a `// row N` comment on each assertion.\n\nYou will mostly be hand-crafting corrupt PNG byte streams. Write a small helper to build a stream from a list of (chunk_name, payload) with correct or deliberately WRONG CRCs — the PNG signature is `[137,80,78,71,13,10,26,10]`, each chunk is `be_u32(len) || name(4) || data || be_u32(crc32(name||data))`. You can compute CRC32 with the exported `png_reset_crc` + `png_calculate_crc`… but those give no getter, so implement a 10-line CRC-32 in Rust instead (standard zlib polynomial 0xEDB88320).\n\nThe surface to attack (feed each stream to a reader via `common::src_set` + `png_read_info`/`png_read_image`/`png_read_end`, and ALSO to a progressive reader via `png_set_progressive_read_fn` + `png_process_data`):\n- `png_read_sig`: not a PNG signature; a signature mangled by ASCII/CRLF conversion (`\"\\x89PNG\\r\\n\\x1a\\n\"` with `\\r\\n` → `\\n`); an EBCDIC-mangled signature.\n- `png_read_chunk_header`: length > `PNG_UINT_31_MAX`; a bad chunk-name byte (non-alphabetic); a length that runs past the end of the buffer.\n- `png_crc_finish` / `png_crc_read` / `png_crc_finish_critical`: a wrong CRC in a critical chunk and in an ancillary chunk, under each `png_set_crc_action` setting.\n- `png_get_uint_31` with a value > 0x7fffffff.\n- `png_handle_*` for EVERY chunk: too-short and too-long payloads, duplicated chunks, chunks in the wrong order/place (before IHDR, after IDAT, PLTE for a grayscale image, tRNS for a colour type that forbids it, bKGD/hIST/sBIT/sCAL/pCAL/oFFs/pHYs/tIME/gAMA/cHRM/sRGB/iCCP/sPLT/eXIf/cICP/cLLI/mDCV each with an invalid payload), an IHDR with each invalid field, a zero-length IDAT, an IDAT before IHDR, a missing IEND, an IEND with a non-zero length.\n- `png_handle_sPLT` (5 sites) and `png_handle_unknown` (5 sites) and `png_handle_iCCP` and `png_handle_PLTE` and `png_handle_chunk`: drive each of their distinct rejection branches.\n- `png_inflate_claim` / `png_zlib_inflate` / `png_read_IDAT_data`: corrupt zlib stream, wrong zlib window bits, truncated deflate data, an Adler-32 mismatch (also with `png_set_option(PNG_IGNORE_ADLER32, ON)`), a too-large inflated size vs `png_set_chunk_malloc_max`.\n- `png_combine_row` errors.\n- `pngpread.c`: `png_push_read_sig`, `png_push_read_chunk`, `png_push_read_IDAT`, `png_process_IDAT_data`, `png_push_save_buffer`, `png_push_process_row`, `png_process_data_skip` — reached by feeding truncated/corrupt data to `png_process_data`, calling `png_process_data` after the end, calling `png_process_data_skip` with nothing to skip, and passing size 0 / a NULL buffer.\n- `pngrio.c` / `pngwio.c`: `png_read_data` / `png_write_data` / `png_default_read_data` / `png_default_write_data` / `png_default_flush` with NO read/write function installed (`png_set_read_fn(pp, NULL, None)`), and `png_set_read_fn` called on a WRITE struct and `png_set_write_fn` called on a READ struct (both produce a specific `png_error`).\n\n**Also cover the generic boundaries**: `png_process_data` with size 0 and with a NULL buffer; `png_read_row` with both row and display_row NULL; oversized `png_set_chunk_malloc_max`/`png_set_chunk_cache_max` boundaries (0, 1, `usize::MAX`); a chunk count exactly at and one past `png_set_chunk_cache_max`.\n\n## Rules\n- Never call the Rust crate directly — everything through `dlsym` on both `.so`s.\n- Create a FRESH png_struct inside each `capture`.\n- Never compare raw heap pointer VALUES — compare null-ness, contents, sizes.\n- **The C is ALWAYS correct. Any C↔Rust divergence is a Rust bug: leave the test FAILING, do NOT modify `src/`, do NOT weaken or `#[ignore]` an assertion.** Report it precisely.\n- Build/run from `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-SS8HRb/translation`:\n  `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test t_err4 2>&1 | tail -60`\n  (`--offline` mandatory: no network. `--release` mandatory.)\n- Other agents are concurrently running cargo here; if cargo blocks on the build lock, wait/retry.\n- Iterate until your file compiles cleanly.\n\n## Report back\n1. A list mapping EVERY row number in `E4.md` to the `#[test]` name covering it, or \"unreachable: <reason>\".\n2. Every FAILING test with the exact divergence (input, C result + log, Rust result + log).","uuid":"6e09c01b-e02a-44d5-a7f7-bee7f3bb246f","session_id":"814b2895-9042-4f5f-bd73-35bea46615cb"}
