{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Reg8mtjkjMawEAiyTM2pRq","type":"tool_result","content":"zlib.rs\nsrc/types.rs:52:/// PNG_RELEASE_BUILD == (PNG_LIBPNG_BUILD_BASE_TYPE >= PNG_LIBPNG_BUILD_RC)\nsrc/types.rs:53:pub const PNG_RELEASE_BUILD: bool = PNG_LIBPNG_BUILD_BASE_TYPE >= PNG_LIBPNG_BUILD_RC;\nsrc/pngread_a.rs:61:        /* PNG_RELEASE_BUILD is false in this build, so\nsrc/pngwrite_a.rs:593:        /* PNG_RELEASE_BUILD is false in this build. */\n---\n# ERRORS.md — error-surface table (derived mechanically from `c_src/src/*.c`)\n\nEvery row is ONE distinct rejection site in the C source, found with:\n\n```\ngrep -nE '\\b(png_error|png_chunk_error|png_benign_error|png_app_error|png_warning|png_app_warning|png_chunk_warning|png_chunk_report|png_fixed_error|png_longjmp)[ ]*\\(' c_src/src/*.c\n```\n\n392 sites total.  There are **no `assert`s** anywhere in the library\n(`grep -rn assert c_src/src` finds only comments), so every rejection is one of\nthese calls or a sentinel return (see the sentinel section at the end).\n\nHow the \"expected C result\" is observed in the differential tests: both libraries get an\n`error_fn`/`warning_fn` installed with `png_set_error_fn`, which records the exact message\nbytes; the error callback then unwinds (panic, standing in for the app's `longjmp`).  A test\nasserts C and Rust produce (a) the same sequence of recorded (kind, message) pairs and\n(b) the same return value / `png_image.warning_or_error` + `png_image.message`.\n\nLegend for \"expected C result\": see the table right below; `msg` is the message column.\n\n| macro | expected C behaviour |\n|---|---|\n| `png_error` | FATAL: error_fn(msg) then longjmp/abort — never returns |\n| `png_chunk_error` | FATAL: error_fn(\"<chunkname>: msg\") then longjmp |\n| `png_fixed_error` | FATAL: error_fn(\"fixed point overflow in <s>\") |\n| `png_longjmp` | FATAL: longjmp_fn(jmp_buf, val) / PNG_ABORT |\n| `png_benign_error` | FATAL if flags&BENIGN_*_ERRORS_WARN==0 else warning_fn(msg) |\n| `png_app_error` | FATAL unless flags&APP_WARNINGS_WARN -> warning_fn(msg) |\n| `png_warning` | warning_fn(msg), returns normally |\n| `png_app_warning` | warning_fn(msg), returns normally |\n| `png_chunk_warning` | warning_fn(\"<chunkname>: msg\") |\n| `png_chunk_report` | PNG_CHUNK_ERROR->png_chunk_error / WARNING->png_chunk_warning / benign |\n\n## Rejection sites\n\n| # | function (file:line) | macro | trigger (guard in the C source) | message / expected C result | test |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `png_set_sig_bytes` (png.c:66) | `png_error` | `if (nb > 8)` | \"Too many bytes for PNG signature\" | [ ] |\n| 2 | `PNG_FUNCTION` (png.c:120) | `png_warning` | `if (size != 0 && items >= (~(png_alloc_size_t)0) / size) {` | \"Potential overflow in png_zalloc()\" | [ ] |\n| 3 | `png_user_version_check` (png.c:245) | `png_warning` | `(unconditional at that point)` | \"\" | [ ] |\n| 4 | `png_data_freer` (png.c:479) | `png_error` | `else if (freer == PNG_USER_WILL_FREE_DATA) info_ptr->free_me &= ~mask; else` | \"Unknown freer parameter in png_data_freer\" | [ ] |\n| 5 | `png_convert_to_rfc1123` (png.c:802) | `png_warning` | `if (png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer(png_ptr->time_buffer, ptime) == 0)` | \"Ignoring invalid time value\" | [ ] |\n| 6 | `png_set_rgb_coefficients` (png.c:1938) | `png_error` | `if (r+g+b != 32768)` | \"internal error handling cHRM coefficients\" | [ ] |\n| 7 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:1971) | `png_warning` | `if (width == 0) {` | \"Image width is zero in IHDR\" | [ ] |\n| 8 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:1977) | `png_warning` | `if (width > PNG_UINT_31_MAX) {` | \"Invalid image width in IHDR\" | [ ] |\n| 9 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:2007) | `png_warning` | `(unconditional at that point)` | \"Image width is too large for this architecture\" | [ ] |\n| 10 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:2017) | `png_warning` | `if (width > PNG_USER_WIDTH_MAX) #endif {` | \"Image width exceeds user limit in IHDR\" | [ ] |\n| 11 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:2023) | `png_warning` | `if (height == 0) {` | \"Image height is zero in IHDR\" | [ ] |\n| 12 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:2029) | `png_warning` | `if (height > PNG_UINT_31_MAX) {` | \"Invalid image height in IHDR\" | [ ] |\n| 13 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:2039) | `png_warning` | `if (height > PNG_USER_HEIGHT_MAX) #endif {` | \"Image height exceeds user limit in IHDR\" | [ ] |\n| 14 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:2047) | `png_warning` | `if (bit_depth != 1 && bit_depth != 2 && bit_depth != 4 && bit_depth != 8 && bit_depth != 16) {` | \"Invalid bit depth in IHDR\" | [ ] |\n| 15 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:2054) | `png_warning` | `if (color_type < 0 \\|\\| color_type == 1 \\|\\| color_type == 5 \\|\\| color_type > 6) {` | \"Invalid color type in IHDR\" | [ ] |\n| 16 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:2063) | `png_warning` | `color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_GRAY_ALPHA \\|\\| color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_RGB_ALPHA) && bit_depth < 8)) {` | \"Invalid color type/bit depth combination in IHDR\" | [ ] |\n| 17 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:2069) | `png_warning` | `if (interlace_type >= PNG_INTERLACE_LAST) {` | \"Unknown interlace method in IHDR\" | [ ] |\n| 18 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:2075) | `png_warning` | `if (compression_type != PNG_COMPRESSION_TYPE_BASE) {` | \"Unknown compression method in IHDR\" | [ ] |\n| 19 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:2091) | `png_warning` | `if ((png_ptr->mode & PNG_HAVE_PNG_SIGNATURE) != 0 && png_ptr->mng_features_permitted != 0)` | \"MNG features are not allowed in a PNG datastream\" | [ ] |\n| 20 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:2101) | `png_warning` | `(color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_RGB \\|\\| color_type == PNG_COLOR_TYPE_RGB_ALPHA))) {` | \"Unknown filter method in IHDR\" | [ ] |\n| 21 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:2107) | `png_warning` | `if ((png_ptr->mode & PNG_HAVE_PNG_SIGNATURE) != 0) {` | \"Invalid filter method in IHDR\" | [ ] |\n| 22 | `png_check_IHDR` (png.c:2115) | `png_warning` | `if (filter_type != PNG_FILTER_TYPE_BASE) {` | \"Unknown filter method in