{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_rhkczzbpw7v5p37p2mbz5bn2m3vcws77o34ta4pigdltrlpdn3iq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`translation/tests/t_pure.rs` is written and green: **22 tests, 0 failures** (`cargo test --offline --release --test t_pure`). Only that file was created; nothing else was touched.\n\n## Rows covered → test names\n\n| Row | `#[test]` name | Cases |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 version/copyright strings | `r01_version_numbers_and_strings` | 2 (NULL + real `png_structp`), full `CStr` compare + absolute checks (10659, `1.6.59.git`) |\n| 2 save/get uint | `r02_save_and_get_uint_roundtrip` | 4103 (4096 random + 0,1,0x7fffffff,0x80000000,0xffffffff,…); compares all 3 buffers and all 4 readers |\n| 3 `png_get_uint_31` | `r03_get_uint_31` | 2055 (2048 random ≤0x7fffffff + 3 error-path values → identical `png_error`) |\n| 4 `png_muldiv` | `r04_muldiv` | 6873 (729 edge triples incl. 0 divisor, ±1, MIN/MAX + 6144 random); compares ret **and** `res` (sentinel-prefilled, so \"did not write\" is also compared) |\n| 5 reciprocal | `r05_reciprocal` | 6208 pairs, both argument orders |\n| 6 gamma correct | `r06_gamma_correct` | 1606 (73 gammas incl. 100000/45455/220000/1/1000000 × v boundaries and randoms) |\n| 7 gamma table | `r07_build_and_destroy_gamma_table` | 144 (bit_depth 8/16 × gamma/alpha-mode combos) |\n| 8 exported arrays | `r08_sRGB_tables` | 256 + 512 + 512 elements, element-wise |\n| 9 XYZ↔xy | `r09_XYZ_from_xy_and_back` | 2002 xy + 1202 XYZ (sRGB primaries, perturbations, random, full-range); compares ret + all 9/8 fields |\n| 10 fp parsing | `r10_check_fp_number_and_string` | 1123 (all hand-picked strings × sizes len-1/len/len+1/0 + 500 random from the given alphabet); compares ret, `state`, `whereami`, `png_check_fp_string` |\n| 11 `png_ascii_from_fp` | `r11_ascii_from_fp` | 756 (14 fixed values × precision 0..16 + 500 randoms + 18 buffer-too-small → identical `png_error`); whole 32-byte buffer |\n| 12 `png_ascii_from_fixed` | `r12_ascii_from_fixed` | 1556 incl. i32::MIN/MAX, 0, ±1 and too-small buffers |\n| 13 `png_fixed`/`_ITU` | `r13_fixed_conversions` | 1223 doubles each, in-range and out-of-range (`png_fixed_error` log compared) |\n| 14 | `r14a_safecat` (2698), `r14b_format_number` (712), `r14c_warning_parameters_and_formatted_warning` (1468) | safecat: bufsize 0..17 × pos 0..18 × strings + NULL buf/str; format_number: formats 0..6 × 16 numbers + 600 randoms, compares returned **offset** + buffer; 14c: full 8×32 parameter block + the emitted warning text |\n| 15 | `r15a_convert_to_rfc1123` (1919), `r15b_convert_from_time_t` (513), `r15c_convert_from_struct_tm` (396) | all months incl. 0/13, day 1/31, hour 0/23, min 0/59, sec 0/60, 400 random `png_time`s; `png_convert_to_rfc1123` string + \"Ignoring invalid time value\" warning |\n| 16 `png_sig_cmp` | `r16_sig_cmp` | 3800: correct signature, every single-byte corruption (0, 0xff, ±1) × `start` 0..9 × `num` 0..9 + randoms |\n| 17 `png_check_IHDR` | `r17_check_IHDR` | 6563: exhaustive bd 0..17 × ct 0..7 × il 0..2 × cm × ft for two (w,h) pairs, all 7×7 (w,h) pairs, 3000 random combos, negative ct, filter 64 |\n| 18 grayscale palette | `r18_build_grayscale_palette` | 18 bit depths + NULL palette; all 256 entries (sentinel-prefilled) |\n\n## Failing tests\nNone. **No divergence found between the C and Rust libraries** in any of these ~48,000 differential cases.\n\n## Notes / caveats\n- **Row 7 (documented in the file):** there is no exported getter for the gamma tables, so the test verifies the *observable* effect: gamma values are installed via `png_set_gamma_fixed`/`png_set_alpha_mode_fixed` (their app-warnings/app-errors must match), a second `png_build_gamma_table` without a destroy must emit \"gamma table being rebuilt\" in both (proving the pointers were set), and a build *after* `png_destroy_gamma_table` must **not** warn (proving the destroy cleared them), plus `png_destroy_gamma_table` idempotence — for bit_depth 8 and 16.\n- **Row 6:** `png_gamma_correct` dispatches on `png_struct::bit_depth`, which is 0 for a fresh reader, so it exercises the 16-bit path only (there is no public way to set `bit_depth` without a real read). Gammas are kept ≥ 0 because a negative gamma makes the C compute a double outside the return type's range, which is C UB.\n- **`png_xy` field order** is `redx,redy,greenx,greeny,bluex,bluey,whitex,whitey` (per `c_src/include/pngstruct.h`), *not* whitex-first as the task text suggested; the local `#[repr(C)]` struct follows the header.\n- **Environment gotcha (affects the other test files too):** `c_src/build/libpng.so` is linked **without `-lm`** (undefined `floor`, `pow`, `modf`, `frexp`), so any test binary that reaches libpng's float code dies with `symbol lookup error: undefined symbol: floor`. `t_pure.rs` fixes this locally by `dlopen`ing `libm.so.6` with `RTLD_NOW|RTLD_GLOBAL` (`ensure_libm()`, called at the top of every test). `cargo test --release` for the whole suite currently fails in `t_write` for exactly this reason — those files (or the C build, or `tests/common/mod.rs`) need the same trick; I could not touch them.\n- `diff()` prints a `STATS <row>: N cases, K png_error, M with messages` line (visible with `--nocapture`) confirming each row really reaches its error/warning paths."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":445,"cache_read_input_tokens":157558,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":445,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_015Vpu62jt87qW7L9e5oxiyH","session_id":"814b2895-9042-4f5f-bd73-35bea46615cb","uuid":"a11c70d9-7251-4f33-afcc-02880c92f8a4","timestamp":"2026-09-08T15:33:34.193Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write t_pure.rs differential tests"}
