{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a5c6a9b43ac59710d","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01PQfRb2Q8dDXpt8Mp1yGda7","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-6wP1XG/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-SS8HRb/814b2895-9042-4f5f-bd73-35bea46615cb/tasks/a5c6a9b43ac59710d.output","summary":"Compiles clean with no warnings and all 10 tests pass.\n\n## Report\n\n**File created:** `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-SS8HRb/translation/tests/t_write.rs` (only that file was touched).\n\n### 1. Rows covered → test names\n\n| CONFIGS.md row | `#[test]` |\n|---|---|\n| 28 low-level chunk writers called directly | `cfg28_chunk_writers` |\n| 29 `png_write_png` one-shot | `cfg29_write_png_oneshot` |\n| 30 `png_write_info` + row/rows/image + `png_write_end` | `cfg30_lowlevel_pipeline` |\n| 31 `png_set_filter` | `cfg31_set_filter` |\n| 32 zlib level/strategy/window/mem | `cfg32_compression_params` |\n| 33 `png_set/get_compression_buffer_size` | `cfg33_compression_buffer_size` |\n| 34 `png_set_flush` / `png_write_flush` | `cfg34_flush` |\n| 35 text chunks + `png_set_text_compression_*` | `cfg35_text_chunks` |\n| 36 all ancillary chunks singly and combined | `cfg36_ancillary_chunks` |\n| 37 unknown chunks / keep / location / `png_handle_as_unknown` | `cfg37_unknown_chunks` |\n\n**3538 distinct write configurations**, ~3.95 MB of PNG output compared byte-for-byte (plus flush counts and message logs). Runtime 0.38 s.\n\n### 2. Failing tests / divergences\n\n**None. C and Rust agree on every one of the 3538 configurations** — identical byte streams, identical flush counts, identical error/warning logs (including all `png_error` unwind points such as `\"no rows for png_write_image to write\"`, `\"Unknown custom filter method\"`, `\"invalid compression buffer size\"`, `\"text compression mode is out of range\"`, `\"Invalid sCAL height\"`, `\"zTXt: invalid compression type\"`, `\"iTXt: invalid compression\"`, `\"Unrecognized equation type for pCAL chunk\"`, `\"ICC profile too short\"`, `\"Invalid number of colors in palette\"`, `\"buffer error\"`).\n\nI verified the comparison is not vacuous: a negative-control run that flipped one bit of the Rust output made all 10 tests fail with the exact offset reported (`[28.sig+IHDR+IEND ct=0 bd=1 il=0 1x1] output differs at byte offset 37 (C len 45, Rust len 45)`). `cmp()` also asserts that each configuration produced *something* (bytes or a message), and a `T_WRITE_TRACE=1` env var dumps per-configuration byte/flush/log summaries.\n\n### 3. Notes, workarounds and gaps\n\n* **`tests/common/api.rs` has three wrong prototypes.** I did not edit it; I declared correct local versions in `mod lo` inside my file. Calling the shipped declarations would corrupt the argument registers:\n  * `png_write_cICP` — C takes `(png_structrp, png_byte, png_byte, png_byte, png_byte)`, api.rs declares `(png_structp, *const png_byte)`.\n  * `png_write_iCCP` — C takes `(png_structrp, png_const_charp, png_const_bytep, png_uint_32)`, api.rs omits the length.\n  * `png_write_zTXt` — C takes `(png_structrp, key, text, int compression)`, api.rs inserts a bogus `len: usize` before `compression`.\n* **`png_xy`** defined locally `#[repr(C)]` in field order from `c_src/include/pngstruct.h:74` (`redx, redy, greenx, greeny, bluex, bluey, whitex, whitey`).\n* **libm workaround (environmental, not a translation bug).** `c_src/build/libpng.so` has undefined `floor/pow/frexp/modf` but **no `DT_NEEDED` for libm**, while the Rust cdylib does link libm privately. Any test touching the floating-point APIs (`png_set_gAMA`, `png_set_cHRM`, `png_set_sCAL`, …) died with `symbol lookup error: … undefined symbol: floor`. `need_libm()` dlopens `libm.so.6` with `RTLD_GLOBAL` before the first `libs()` call. (Another agent's `t_mem` has an equivalent `t_mem_libm_is_linked` test, so this is a known repo-wide issue.)\n* **Not tested / deliberately excluded:**\n  * `png_write_pCAL` equation type 4 and above only reach the `png_error` path (there are just 4 defined types, 0..3); \"all 5 equation types\" is covered as types 0..4 with 4 asserting the error.\n  * `png_set_pCAL` types 0..3 only — `png_set_pCAL` rejects type ≥ 4 in `pngset.c` before anything is written, so the write side cannot see it.\n  * `png_write_sCAL_s`/`png_set_sCAL_s` with unit 0 or negative dimensions is only exercised as an error/warning path (libpng rejects it in the setter).\n  * `png_set_filter_heuristics*` (row 31 does not mention them; they are no-op stubs in 1.6).\n  * MNG intrapixel filter 64 (`png_permit_mng_features`) is only touched via the \"invalid filter type\" IHDR warning case, since row 28 does not call for MNG.\n* **Non-obvious observations while writing the tests** (both libraries behave identically, so these are just coverage notes): `png_set_unknown_chunks` hard-errors on `location == 0`, so row 37's `png_set_unknown_chunk_location` cases must pre-seed a valid location; `png_set_unknown_chunk_location` silently ignores out-of-range indices; and `png_set_flush(n)` combined with explicit `png_write_flush` mid-image reproducibly ends in zlib `\"buffer error\"` for n ∈ {1,2} in **both** libraries.","usage":{"total_tokens":179568,"tool_uses":57,"duration_ms":975359},"uuid":"4ae0da08-538e-4a3a-9881-d69bbaa6f497","session_id":"814b2895-9042-4f5f-bd73-35bea46615cb"}
