{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_q6slbtbc5e4di2hf4rlnyf6yyltz5bq4eqwate5gpi3xyz6ptmla","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-SS8HRb/translation/tests/t_mem.rs` (2505 lines, 20 tests, compiles warning-free). Only that file was created/modified.\n\n`timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test t_mem` → **18 passed, 2 failed**.\n\n## 1. Row coverage → test names\n\n| Row | Tests |\n|---|---|\n| 52 | `cfg52_custom_allocator_write_sequence`, `cfg52_custom_allocator_read_sequence`, `cfg52_malloc_family`, `cfg52_get_mem_ptr` |\n| 53 | `cfg53_create_destroy_info_struct`, `cfg53_info_init_3`, `cfg53_free_data_masks`, `cfg53_free_data_rows_owned`, `cfg53_data_freer` |\n| 57 | `cfg57_icc_check_length`, `cfg57_icc_check_header`, `cfg57_icc_check_tag_table`, `cfg57_resolve_file_gamma` |\n| 66 | `cfg66_calculate_crc_direct`, `cfg66_crc_action_affects_calculate_crc`, `cfg66_zstream_helpers` |\n| 67 | `cfg67_read_chunk_header`, `cfg67_handle_chunk_sweep`, `cfg67_handle_unknown_keep` |\n| infra | `t_mem_libm_is_linked` (see §3) |\n\nEach sweep carries non-vacuity assertions (e.g. `cfg67_handle_chunk_sweep` asserts all four `png_handle_result_code` values are actually reached; the ICC sweeps assert both accepted/rejected/unwound/warned cases occur; the CRC test asserts the emitted CRC bytes actually vary).\n\n## 2. Failing tests — the divergence\n\n`cfg52_custom_allocator_write_sequence` and `cfg52_custom_allocator_read_sequence` both fail on **one** root cause:\n\n```\nread/write: sizeof(png_struct) handed to the user malloc_fn differs (C first)\n  left: 1232      right: 1224\n```\n\nFull recorded sequences (only element 0 differs; the tests deliberately compare the tail first, and it matches element-for-element):\n- write: `[1232|1224, 352, 448, 27, 62, 5952, 1024, 1024, 65536, 65536, 37, 37, 37, 37, 8200, 5952, 2048, 2048, 65536, 65536]`\n- read: `[1232|1224, 352, 25, 448, 27, 64, 7160, 61, 62, 117, 117, 270, 512]`\n\n**Root cause (Rust bug, located precisely).** `c_src/include/pngstruct.h:376-381`:\n```c\n#if defined(PNG_READ_EXPAND_SUPPORTED) && \\\n    (defined(PNG_ARM_NEON_IMPLEMENTATION) || defined(PNG_RISCV_RVV_IMPLEMENTATION))\n   png_bytep riffled_palette;\n#endif\n```\n`pngpriv.h` unconditionally `#define`s both macros (to `0` on x86-64 — `pngpriv.h:170` and `:312`), and `#ifdef` is satisfied by a `0` value, so the C `png_struct` **does** contain `riffled_palette`, verified at offset 1040 (`mng_features_permitted` sits at 1048, not 1040). `translation/src/pngstruct.rs::png_struct` has no `riffled_palette` field at all (`grep -r riffled translation/src` → no hits), making it 8 bytes shorter.\n\nThis is observable through the public API: it is the byte count passed to an application-supplied `png_malloc_ptr`. Fix = add `pub riffled_palette: png_bytep,` between `rgb_to_gray_green_coeff` and `mng_features_permitted` in `src/pngstruct.rs`. Left failing as instructed; nothing was weakened or ignored.\n\nEverything else matched exactly, including `sizeof(png_info)` (352 on both), the entire read/write allocation *pattern*, all `png_free_data`/`png_data_freer` state vectors, all ICC messages, all chunk-handling result codes and message logs.\n\n## 3. Things worth flagging\n\n- **`c_src/build/libpng.so` is linked without `-lm`** (its cmake flags are just `-std=gnu99 -fPIC`), so `floor`/`frexp` are undefined in it and the *test binary* must supply libm. Without that the process dies with `symbol lookup error: ... undefined symbol: floor` as soon as any float path runs. I added a `#[link(name = \"m\")]` block + `t_mem_libm_is_linked` to force libm into `t_mem`'s `DT_NEEDED`. **The sibling test files `t_err2.rs` (and probably `t_err1/t_err3/t_simple/...`, which appeared in `tests/` while I was working) hit exactly this crash** — `cargo test --release` aborts in `t_err2` with the same error. They need the same fix, but I'm not permitted to touch them.\n- **`tests/common/api.rs` declares `png_icc_check_header/_length/_tag_table` with a bogus extra `colorspace` argument.** This libpng (1.6.59) has no `png_colorspace` type at all (`grep png_colorspace c_src/include/*.h` → nothing; the struct was removed from `pngstruct.h`), and the real prototypes in `pngpriv.h:1886-1900` take no such parameter. Using the harness declarations would shift every argument. I declared the correct signatures locally in `mod x`. **Consequence for row 57 as specified: there is no colorspace struct to zero/compare** — the tests compare the return value + full message log only, across 3 struct flavours (reader / writer / reader with `png_set_benign_errors(0)`, which flips the benign path from warning to `png_error`).\n- **`tests/common/mod.rs` `PNG_FREE_*` constants are wrong** (e.g. `PNG_FREE_TEXT = 0x0200`, but `png.h:1850` says `0x4000`; `PNG_FREE_ALL = 0x7FFF` vs `0xffff`). I defined the authoritative values locally as `FREE_*`. Other tests using `common::PNG_FREE_*` are silently testing the wrong masks.\n- **`png_reset_crc`/`png_calculate_crc` have no direct observation point** (`png_struct::crc` is private). Solved without weakening: `png_write_chunk_start` does `png_reset_crc` + `png_calculate_crc(name,4)` and `png_write_chunk_end` emits `png_ptr->crc`, so extra `png_reset_crc`/`png_calculate_crc` calls injected in between are fully visible in the sink bytes. Lengths 0/1/2/255/4096 × 7 injection scenarios × ancillary/critical name, plus a 6×6 `png_set_crc_action` grid that exercises the `need_crc == 0` branch.\n- **`png_zalloc`'s overflow guard is unreachable on 64-bit**: `items >= SIZE_MAX/size` requires `items >= 2^32+1`, impossible for `uInt`. `(0xFFFFFFFF, 0xFFFFFFFF)` therefore reaches the allocation-failure path (`png_warning \"Out of memory\"`), not the overflow warning. Noted in a comment; both paths compared.\n- **`cfg67` streams carry no trailing IEND**: `pngrutil.c`'s `read_chunks` table gives IEND `pos_after = PNG_AFTER_IDAT`, so an IEND with no preceding IDAT is a critical \"out of place\" error that unwinds before the trace can be collected. The loop instead runs exactly `1 + n` chunks and then samples `png_get_valid`/unknown count/text count/`png_get_io_state`/`src_pos`.\n- **Unknown-chunk names must have an upper-case third byte** (`check_chunk_name` does not clear bit 5 of the reserved byte), so `uNkN` is rejected as `bad header (invalid type)`; the tests use `uNKn` (ancillary) and `UnKn` (critical).\n- `cfg53_data_freer` populates the info struct **without** `png_set_rows`: handing `PNG_FREE_ROWS`/`PNG_FREE_ALL` ownership to libpng while the rows are app-owned makes libpng `free()` Rust-owned memory (this reproducibly aborted with `malloc_consolidate(): unaligned fastbin chunk`). Owned rows get their own scenario, `cfg53_free_data_rows_owned`, with rows allocated via `png_malloc`.\n- `png_info_init_3` is tested with the exact C `sizeof(png_info)` (352, measured by compiling against `pngpriv.h`) plus 351/0/1/8/4096/`usize::MAX`; it must be driven on a struct **without** a user allocator because it uses the system `free`/`malloc` directly."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":520,"cache_read_input_tokens":240231,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":520,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Vd7RCgzqQMCnW9rPtUEPZ6","session_id":"814b2895-9042-4f5f-bd73-35bea46615cb","uuid":"11019889-b615-4ae8-b83d-61381cab68d8","timestamp":"2026-09-08T15:43:47.064Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write t_mem.rs differential tests"}
