{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"ac0af778c6d0e82df","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01LbBxjEteijbrPPa5EWUuMx","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-6wP1XG/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-SS8HRb/814b2895-9042-4f5f-bd73-35bea46615cb/tasks/ac0af778c6d0e82df.output","summary":"Done. Created `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-SS8HRb/translation/tests/t_simple.rs` (2170 lines, the only file touched). **18 tests, all passing, 4.5 s** with `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test t_simple`.\n\n## 1. Row coverage → test names\n\n| Row | Tests |\n|---|---|\n| 59 (read from memory) | `cfg59_read_from_memory_full_matrix`, `cfg59_read_from_memory_large_images`, `cfg59_read_from_memory_padded_stride_and_flags`, `cfg59_read_from_memory_truncated_and_corrupt` |\n| 60 (read from file/stdio) | `cfg60_read_from_file_and_stdio`, `cfg60_read_from_missing_file` |\n| 61 (write to memory) | `cfg61_write_to_memory_matrix`, `cfg61_write_to_memory_padded_stride_and_flags`, `cfg61_write_to_memory_colormap_entry_counts`, `cfg61_write_then_read_roundtrip` |\n| 62 (write to file/stdio) | `cfg62_write_to_file_and_stdio`, `cfg62_write_to_unwritable_path` |\n| 63 (`png_image_free`/`png_image_error`) | `cfg63_free_after_successful_read`, `cfg63_free_after_failed_read`, `cfg63_free_on_zeroed_and_bad_version_image`, `cfg63_invalid_argument_paths`, `cfg63_png_image_error_direct`, `cfg63_warning_paths_preserve_state` |\n\nScale actually exercised (printed by each test as a `[cfg…] Tally{…}` line): **67,000+ differential read configurations** and **1,670 write configurations**.\n\n- Inputs are built with the low-level **C** writer: all 15 valid colour-type/bit-depth pairs × interlaced/not × sizes 33×5, 1×1, sub-byte widths 2/3/5/7/9, tiny interlaced 1×1/2×3/5×1/1×7/4×4, tRNS variants, 7 gAMA/sRGB variants, plus 6 large (64×48/47×33) images — 128 inputs total.\n- Output cross-product: all 36 formats ({GRAY,GA,AG,RGB,BGR,RGBA,ARGB,BGRA,ABGR} × {8-bit,LINEAR} × {direct,COLORMAP}) × `row_stride` ∈ {0 (defaulted), +natural, −natural, ±(natural+pad)} × `background` ∈ {NULL, mid, black, white}.\n- Compared per configuration: both return values, `cmp_key()` after *each* call, the **whole** output buffer (allocated at `PNG_IMAGE_SIZE`-equivalent, pre-filled with a fixed non-zero pattern plus guard bytes), the colormap buffer (256-entry max, always passed, so it is also checked to be *untouched* for non-colormap formats), the harness message log, and my ported `PNG_IMAGE_SIZE`/`PNG_IMAGE_COLORMAP_SIZE` values.\n- Write side compares return value, `*memory_bytes`, `cmp_key()` and the produced PNG bytes for all three modes (`memory==NULL` query, exact size, one byte short) and cross-checks file vs stdio vs memory output byte-for-byte.\n\n## 2. Failing tests / divergences\n\n**None.** C and Rust agreed on every one of the ~69,000 configurations, including error/warning messages, `warning_or_error` bits, colormap contents and every untouched buffer byte.\n\nI verified the harness is not vacuous:\n- Each test asserts a minimum success rate and that every successful decode actually wrote to the buffer (`Tally::check`); e.g. `cfg59 full matrix` = 55,296 configs, 55,296 opened, 54,972 decoded, 54,969 wrote output. The 324 rejected ones are the legitimate `\"background color must be supplied to remove alpha/transparency\"` path (identical in both libraries).\n- Write tests assert every configuration produced a PNG signature and that the one-byte-short case returns 0 while still reporting the full size.\n- **Mutation check:** temporarily negating the Rust-side `row_stride` made `cfg59_read_from_memory_padded_stride_and_flags` fail with `first differing byte at offset 0 of 176 / C 427432b0… / RS ebf8021a…`, then reverted.\n\n## 3. Caveats / things I could not test\n\n- **Environment fix-up (important):** `c_src/build/libpng.so` is linked **without `-lm`** — `pow`, `floor`, `frexp`, `modf` are undefined. Since `libloading` uses `RTLD_LOCAL`, the C library aborted the process (`symbol lookup error: … undefined symbol: floor`) the first time the simplified reader built a gamma table. My `L()` helper `dlopen`s `libm.so.6` with `RTLD_NOW|RTLD_GLOBAL` once, which puts those symbols in the global scope, i.e. makes the C build behave as a normally-linked one. This alters no libpng behaviour, but the C build itself should probably be fixed.\n- `png_image_finish_read`'s `\"image too large\"` and `\"row_stride too large\"` branches are reached by hand-doctoring `image.width`/`image.height` after `begin_read` (in `cfg63_invalid_argument_paths`); they cannot be reached from a real PNG on this machine.\n- `png_safe_execute` / `png_safe_error` / `png_safe_warning` (also named in CONFIGS row 63) are only driven *indirectly*, through the simplified API. Calling them directly requires constructing a `png_control`, whose layout is private and differs between the two builds.\n- The 32/64-bit `PNG_IMAGE_BUFFER_SIZE` overflow guards and `PNG_IMAGE_DATA_SIZE`/`PNG_ZLIB_MAX_SIZE` \"PNG too big\" write path need multi-GB images; not attempted.\n- Cosmetic noise: `thread '<unnamed>' panicked at src/pngerror.rs:15: Box<dyn Any>` lines appear on stderr. That is the Rust crate's longjmp-substitute panic being printed because `common::capture`'s panic-hook suppression is process-global and races with the other tests running in parallel. The panics are caught; no assertion is affected.","usage":{"total_tokens":187353,"tool_uses":64,"duration_ms":1320308},"uuid":"d5dfc81a-3230-4c14-a037-3daf9f107859","session_id":"814b2895-9042-4f5f-bd73-35bea46615cb"}
