{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_4ojhe56jp2ilyxbmaev6lbvrjwas2odnbc5l7ckiwamxo7tnhl5q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 30 tests in `translation/tests/t_err1.rs` pass; no C↔Rust divergence found. Nothing outside that one file was touched.\n\n## Row → test mapping (all 73 rows of `.verify/E1.md`)\n\nEvery row also has an *exact message text* assertion in `err_e1_exact_message_texts_all_rows` (which asserts the C reference really emits the expected diagnostic before comparing, so no assertion can pass vacuously — this actually caught one wrong assumption of mine: the running version string is `1.6.59.git`, not `1.6.59`).\n\n| rows | test |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | `err_png_c_set_sig_bytes_row_1` |\n| 2 | `err_png_c_zalloc_row_2` — **guard itself unreachable**, fall-through covered |\n| 3 | `err_png_c_user_version_check_row_3` |\n| 4 | `err_png_c_data_freer_row_4`, `err_png_c_free_data_null_sentinels` |\n| 6 | **unreachable** (see below) — no-op path covered by `err_png_c_set_rgb_coefficients_row_6` |\n| 7, 8, 10–18, 19, 20, 21, 23 | `err_png_c_check_ihdr_rows_7_23` (+ `err_pngget_get_ihdr_row_23` reaches row 23 via `png_get_IHDR`) |\n| 9, 22 | **unreachable** |\n| 24, 25 | `err_png_c_ascii_conversion_rows_24_25` |\n| 26, 27, 56 | `err_png_c_fixed_rows_26_27_56` |\n| 28 | **not a rejection site** (png.c:3377 is prose inside a block comment); `png_gamma_correct` still compared in `err_png_c_gamma_rows_28_29` |\n| 29 | `err_png_c_gamma_rows_28_29` |\n| 30, 31 | **unreachable**; reachable `png_image_free` path covered by `err_png_c_image_free_rows_30_31` |\n| 32, 33 | `err_pngerror_c_warning_rows_32_33` |\n| 34, 35, 36, 37, 38 | `err_pngerror_c_benign_error_rows_34_38` |\n| 39, 40, 41 | `err_pngerror_c_app_warning_rows_39_41` |\n| 42, 43, 44 | `err_pngerror_c_app_error_rows_42_44` |\n| 45 | **unreachable** (see below) |\n| 46, 47, 48, 49 | `err_pngerror_c_chunk_diagnostics_rows_45_49` |\n| 50, 51 | `err_pngerror_c_chunk_benign_error_rows_50_51` |\n| 52, 53, 54, 55 | `err_pngerror_c_chunk_report_rows_52_55` |\n| 57 | **unreachable** |\n| 58, 59, 60 | `err_pngerror_c_longjmp_rows_57_60` |\n| 61 | `err_pngget_fixed_inches_row_61` |\n| 62 | `err_pngget_get_eXIf_row_62` |\n| 63, 64 | `err_pngmem_array_rows_63_64` |\n| 65, 66, 67 | `err_pngmem_alloc_rows_65_67` |\n| 280 | `err_pngtrans_set_shift_row_280` |\n| 281, 284 | **unreachable** |\n| 282, 283 | `err_pngtrans_set_filler_rows_281_284` |\n| 285 | `err_pngtrans_user_transform_info_row_285` |\n\nGeneric boundaries live in `err_pngget_null_sentinels` (~90 accessors × {NULL/NULL, pp/NULL, NULL/ip, writer pp/ip, reader pp/ip}, results collected into a comparable `Vec<i64>`) and `err_png_c_free_data_null_sentinels`.\n\n## Unreachable rows and why\n\n- **row 2** `png_zalloc` overflow guard: `items >= SIZE_MAX/size` with `items`,`size` both 32-bit `uInt` and `png_alloc_size_t` 64-bit ⇒ dead on any 64-bit target.\n- **row 6** `png_set_rgb_coefficients`: labelled \"internal error\" in the C; the `r+g+b <= 32769` guard plus the `add` fix-up always drive the sum to exactly 32768, and it only runs at all with chromaticities read from a cHRM/mDCV chunk.\n- **row 9** \"Image width is too large for this architecture\": needs width > ~2.3e18 but width is `png_uint_32`.\n- **row 22** png.c:2115 is the `#else` arm of `PNG_MNG_FEATURES_SUPPORTED`, which this build defines (same message as row 20, which *is* covered).\n- **rows 30, 31** `#else` arms of `PNG_SIMPLIFIED_WRITE/READ_SUPPORTED`, both defined.\n- **row 45** `png_chunk_error(NULL, msg)` → `png_error(NULL)` → `png_default_error` → `png_longjmp(NULL,1)` → `PNG_ABORT()`, i.e. `abort()`. Cannot be observed by a surviving test process, so it is deliberately not called.\n- **row 57** \"Libpng jmp_buf still allocated\" needs `jmp_buf_size == 0` *and* `jmp_buf_ptr != &jmp_buf_local`, a state no exported API can produce.\n- **rows 281, 284** `#else` arms of `PNG_READ_FILLER_SUPPORTED` / `PNG_WRITE_FILLER_SUPPORTED`, both defined.\n\n## Failing tests\n\nNone — C and Rust agree on every message log and every return value/sentinel for all of the above.\n\n## Notes worth passing on\n\n1. `translation/tests/common/mod.rs` does not load libm, and `c_src/build/libpng.so` was linked without `-lm` (`floor`/`pow` undefined, and glibc's `libc.so.6` does not export them). Any test that reaches `png_ascii_from_fp`/`png_fixed`/gamma must `dlopen(\"libm.so.6\", RTLD_GLOBAL)` first; `t_pure.rs` has an `ensure_libm()` helper and I replicated it locally (called from `diff`). Without it the process dies with `symbol lookup error: ... undefined symbol: floor`.\n2. Cosmetic (not an assertion failure): during `png_image_begin_read_from_memory` on junk input the Rust crate prints `thread '<unnamed>' panicked at src/pngerror.rs:15: Box<dyn Any>` to stderr even though `common::capture` installed a silencing panic hook — the crate appears to install/restore a panic hook of its own internally. Observable behaviour matched C exactly.\n3. Two `pngget.c` accessors are UB with a NULL `png_ptr` in the reference C (`png_get_io_state` and `png_get_io_chunk_type` dereference it with no check), so they are exercised with live structs only; this is commented in the file.\n4. `png_free_data(pp, ip, PNG_FREE_TEXT, num)` with an out-of-range `num` indexes `info_ptr->text[num]` unchecked in C, so oversized `num` is only exercised against a freshly created info struct (where every branch is guarded) — also commented."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":887,"cache_read_input_tokens":246640,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":887,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_012M3mdF1NGDE8vXy56KWEEg","session_id":"814b2895-9042-4f5f-bd73-35bea46615cb","uuid":"6461f080-2f2c-4010-ad83-edcee2a4392a","timestamp":"2026-09-08T15:45:07.893Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write t_err1.rs error-path tests"}
