{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a2cba33e9c85d9f8e","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01D8yDYvQFjXi4pay6PRxu1y","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-6wP1XG/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-SS8HRb/814b2895-9042-4f5f-bd73-35bea46615cb/tasks/a2cba33e9c85d9f8e.output","summary":"Created `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-SS8HRb/translation/tests/t_err5.rs` (2206 lines, 37 `#[test]`s). Nothing else was touched.\n\n**`cargo test --offline --release --test t_err5` → 37 passed, 0 failed. No C↔Rust divergence found anywhere in the E5 surface.**\n\n## 1. Row → test mapping (all 103 rows of `.verify/E5.md`)\n\n| rows | `#[test]` |\n|---|---|\n| 290 | `t_row290_zero_length_unknown_chunk` |\n| 291 | `t_row291_mng_features_not_allowed_in_png` |\n| 292 | `t_row292_valid_palette_required` |\n| 296, 297 | `t_rows296_297_write_end` |\n| 301 | `t_row301_row_before_info` |\n| 309 | `t_row309_internal_write_transform_logic_error` (user write-transform that lies about `pixel_depth`) |\n| 310, 312, 313 | `t_rows310_312_313_set_filter` |\n| 314–319 | `t_rows314_319_compression_setters` |\n| 320, 325 | `t_rows320_325_write_png` |\n| 332–336 | `t_rows332_336_image_write_main` |\n| 338 | `t_row338_chunk_length` |\n| 340 | `t_row340_zstream_in_use_by_idat` |\n| 342 | `t_row342_compressed_data_out_short_chain` |\n| 343–351 | `t_rows343_351_write_IHDR` |\n| 352–354 | `t_rows352_354_write_PLTE` |\n| 355 | `t_row355_deflate_claim_failure_for_idat` |\n| 357 | `t_row357_compress_idat_zlib_error` |\n| 358 | `t_row358_write_sRGB` |\n| 359–362, 364, 365 | `t_rows359_365_write_iCCP` |\n| 366 | `t_row366_write_sPLT` |\n| 367–369 | `t_rows367_369_write_sBIT` |\n| 370–373 | `t_rows370_373_write_tRNS` |\n| 374–376 | `t_rows374_376_write_bKGD` |\n| 377 | `t_row377_write_hIST` |\n| 378 | `t_row378_write_tEXt` |\n| 380–382 | `t_rows380_382_write_zTXt` |\n| 383–385 | `t_rows383_385_write_iTXt` |\n| 387 | `t_row387_write_oFFs` |\n| 388, 389 | `t_rows388_389_write_pCAL` |\n| 390 | `t_row390_write_sCAL_s` |\n| 391 | `t_row391_write_pHYs` |\n| 392 | `t_row392_write_tIME` |\n\nPlus 5 non-row tests demanded by the brief: `t_null_pointer_boundaries`, `t_out_of_order_write_sequences`, `t_compression_buffer_size_boundaries`, `t_image_write_to_memory_boundaries`, `t_set_filter_heuristics_are_noops`.\n\n**Unreachable (31 rows)** — reasons are also recorded in the file's module doc comment:\n- **293, 294, 295, 298, 299, 300** — `#else` arms of `PNG_WRITE_{iTXt,zTXt,tEXt}_SUPPORTED`, all defined.\n- **302–308** — guarded by `#if !defined(PNG_WRITE_{INVERT,FILLER,PACKSWAP,PACK,SHIFT,BGR,SWAP}_SUPPORTED)`, all defined.\n- **311** — `#else` arm of `PNG_WRITE_FILTER_SUPPORTED`.\n- **321–324, 326–330** — `#else` arms of the `png_write_png` transform guards. (Row **325** lives *inside* `#ifdef PNG_WRITE_FILLER_SUPPORTED` and **is** covered.)\n- **331** — `png_write_image_16bit`'s `png_error` needs `format` without `FLAG_ALPHA`, but `png_image_write_main` only dispatches there when `alpha != 0`. Dead code.\n- **337** — needs `size > SIZE_MAX - output_bytes` (a ~2^64-byte PNG).\n- **339** — inside `#if PNG_RELEASE_BUILD`, which is **0** here (see below); the `#else` half is row 340.\n- **341** — `deflateEnd` only returns non-`Z_OK` for a `BUSY_STATE` stream; libpng always finishes or abandons the stream before a param change, and returns early while `zowner == png_IDAT`. Only reachable by re-entering libpng from a custom `malloc_fn`.\n- **356** — \"Z_OK on Z_FINISH with output space\"; the `avail_out == 0` case is consumed by the `continue` above it.\n- **363** — the predicate is *character-for-character identical* to row 361's (`png_get_uint_32(profile) != profile_len`), which already `png_error`ed. Dead code.\n- **379, 386** — need a NUL-terminated string > `PNG_UINT_31_MAX` (>2 GiB).\n\n## 2. Failing tests / divergences\n\n**None.** Every assertion (message bytes + order, error-vs-return, emitted byte stream, flush count, return values, `png_image.warning_or_error`/`message`) matched between `c_src/build/libpng.so` and `translation/target/release/liblibpng.so`.\n\n## Key findings worth relaying\n\n1. **`.verify/E5.md`'s `macro` column is misleading for this build.** `PNG_LIBPNG_BUILD_BASE_TYPE == PNG_LIBPNG_BUILD_BETA (2)`, so `PNG_RELEASE_BUILD == 0`. Consequences the tests pin down:\n   - `png_create_write_struct` never sets `PNG_FLAG_APP_WARNINGS_WARN`, and `PNG_BENIGN_WRITE_ERRORS_SUPPORTED` is undefined ⇒ on a write struct `png_app_warning`, `png_app_error` **and** `png_benign_error` are all **fatal** `png_error`s. So rows **297, 312, 370, 371, 372, 373** are FATAL, not warnings.\n   - Row **339** is compiled out and row **340** (`png_error(msg)`) is what fires, with the message `\"zTXt: IDAT using zstream\"`.\n2. **Row 357 is reachable** via two consecutive `png_write_flush()` calls mid-image: zlib returns `Z_BUF_ERROR` (`RANK(flush) <= RANK(old_flush)` with `avail_in == 0`), and the message is zlib's own `\"buffer error\"` (not `\"truncated\"`, because `png_zstream_error` preserves a pre-set `zstream.msg`).\n3. **Row 342 is reachable** only by freeing `png_ptr->zbuffer_list` from inside the application's own write callback (`png_set_compression_buffer_size` from the callback libpng invokes in `png_write_chunk_header`). The test does exactly that and both libraries agree.\n4. **Latent C bug deliberately not tested:** `png_image_write_main` computes `image->height > 0xffffffffU/png_row_stride` without guarding `png_row_stride == 0`, so `png_image_write_to_memory` with `image->width == 0` is an integer division by zero (SIGFPE) in the C reference. Documented in the test file; `width == 0` is excluded so the harness does not abort. Similarly, `png_write_row(pp, NULL)` `memcpy`s from NULL with a valid `pp`, so only the `png_ptr == NULL` path is exercised.\n5. `tests/common/api.rs` declares **`png_write_iCCP`** (missing the 4th `profile_len` arg) and **`png_write_zTXt`** (spurious `len` arg) with signatures that do not match the C ABI; `png_write_cICP` is also wrong (declared as `*const png_byte` instead of four `png_byte`s). I re-declared the two I needed in a local `mod loc` rather than editing the shared file — other E-agents using those wrappers will pass garbage arguments.","usage":{"total_tokens":273143,"tool_uses":62,"duration_ms":1326882},"uuid":"03dba9d5-932e-4814-ba86-ef79eefbe85c","session_id":"814b2895-9042-4f5f-bd73-35bea46615cb"}
