om_fp` will hit the same wall.\n2. `png_get_iCCP` (pngget.c:730) returns `png_get_uint_32(info_ptr->iccp_profile)` rather than the stored `iccp_proflen`, so after `png_set_iCCP` with `proflen < 4` it reads uninitialised heap (nondeterministic, differs per library — not a translation defect). Those cases therefore compare `png_get_valid` only, and no test ever uses a getter-reported length as a slice length.\n3. `png_set_benign_errors` dereferences `png_ptr` with no NULL check in the C, so a NULL `png_ptr` is UB and is deliberately excluded from the NULL-boundary sweep (documented in the test)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":773,"cache_read_input_tokens":272964,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":773,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01AvC22ej2HtCtBLF3dqGgYC","session_id":"814b2895-9042-4f5f-bd73-35bea46615cb","uuid":"53db5a12-4357-484b-828c-dfd5663a7cdf","timestamp":"2026-09-08T15:57:29.236Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write t_err2.rs error-path tests"}
