 — `png_ptr->interlaced` is validated to 0/1 by IHDR.\n- **150, 152, 153, 155** — internal invariants of `png_image_read_background`. In particular row 153 is provably dead: `do_local_background == 2` is only set either from the `mode == PNG_ALPHA_STANDARD` branch (which requires a LINEAR output, contradicting `(format & LINEAR) == 0`) or from the `change & ALPHA` branch (which requires `format` to *lack* ALPHA, contradicting `(format & ALPHA) != 0`).\n- **157, 158, 159** — internal invariants of `png_image_read_direct`; the full `format` sweep (9 sources × 128 format values) inside `image_finish_read_argument_errors` never reaches them.\n- **181** (`png_do_encode_alpha: unexpected call`) — `png_do_encode_alpha` is `static`; `nm -D` shows it exported by *neither* `.so`, so it cannot be driven differentially.\n- **183** (`Uninitialized row`) — requires `row_buf != NULL` with `PNG_FLAG_ROW_INIT == 0`; `row_buf` is only ever allocated by `png_read_start_row`, which sets `ROW_INIT` on the same path, and nothing clears it.\n\n## 2. Failing tests / divergences\n\n**None.** No C↔Rust divergence was found: message bytes, message order, warn-vs-error routing, return values, `png_image::{format,flags,colormap_entries,warning_or_error,message}` and decoded row bytes match exactly in all 50 tests.\n\n## Extra coverage beyond the row list\n`truncated_streams` (empty/1/8-byte/bad-signature/every IHDR prefix), `invalid_ihdr_fields` (18 out-of-range field values), `missing_and_corrupt_chunks` (missing IDAT/IEND, corrupt zlib, corrupt deflate block, mid-row truncation, bad CRC, bad chunk length/type), `read_png_conflicting_transform_bits`, `image_finish_read_argument_errors`, `image_begin_read_from_file_bad_arguments`, `pngread_entry_points_null_{png,info}_ptr`, `rtran_setters_null_png_ptr`, `rtran_setters_on_a_write_struct` (all 24 read-transform setters on a write struct), `filler_and_add_alpha_flags_out_of_range`, `quantize_bad_arguments`, `conflicting_16_bit_transforms` (all 8 scale/strip/expand_16 combinations), `read_row_past_last_row`.\n\n## Notes for whoever else runs tests here (not bugs in the translation)\n1. **`c_src/build/libpng.so` has an unresolved lazy `floor`** (libm not linked). Any test that reaches `convert_gamma_value`/`png_fixed` aborts the whole test binary with `symbol lookup error: ... undefined symbol: floor`. `t_err3.rs` works around this with `ensure_libm()`, which `dlopen`s `libm.so.6` with `RTLD_NOW|RTLD_GLOBAL` *before* `common::libs()` runs. Other error-path test files will hit the same wall.\n2. Three argument ranges named in the task brief are **undefined behaviour in the reference C**, so they are documented in-file rather than asserted: `png_set_read_user_transform_fn(NULL, …)` (pngrtran.c:1133 dereferences `png_ptr` with no NULL guard → SIGSEGV in both libraries); `png_set_quantize` with `num_palette`/`maximum_colors` negative or > 256 (no validation → `png_malloc((size_t)-1)`, `quantize_index[256]` overrun); and `png_set_rgb_to_gray_fixed` with coefficients whose `int` sum overflows (`red + green` wraps, so `PNG_FP_MAX` silently *passes* the range check). `png_read_update_info(pp, NULL)` is likewise UB (`png_read_transform_info` dereferences `info_ptr` immediately).\n3. Two reachability subtleties that cost real digging, recorded as comments in the file: `png_init_rgb_transformations` cancels `PNG_COMPOSE` outright unless the source has alpha or tRNS (so rows 178/179 need an RGBA or palette+tRNS source), and row 106 needs `PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_ALWAYS` for IDAT — with `PNG_HANDLE_CHUNK_NEVER` `png_read_info` rejects the first IDAT as an \"unhandled critical chunk\" before `png_read_end` ever runs.","usage":{"total_tokens":344736,"tool_uses":155,"duration_ms":2218687},"uuid":"7c995351-db90-4d5d-9448-d67e9952fe1d","session_id":"814b2895-9042-4f5f-bd73-35bea46615cb"}
