{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ttju3j523p2hvmahsbszokvixustmguvh2jtgq7kclrwgzp3ygpa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 60 tests pass. Here is the report.\n\n## 1. Rows covered → test names\n\n| Row | `#[test]` |\n|---|---|\n| 38 | `cfg38_read_image_all_shapes`, `cfg38_read_row_variants` (`png_read_row(row,NULL)`, `(NULL,display)`, `(row,display)`, `png_read_rows` with and without display array), `cfg38_read_png_identity`, `cfg38_filter_types` (all 5 adaptive filters + `PNG_ALL_FILTERS`), `cfg38_more_seeds` |\n| 39 | `cfg39_palette_to_rgb`, `_trns_to_alpha`, `_expand`, `_expand_gray_1_2_4_to_8`, `_expand_16`, `_gray_to_rgb`, `_rgb_to_gray_fixed`, `_background_fixed`, `_alpha_mode_fixed`, `_gamma_fixed`, `_quantize`, `_strip_16`, `_scale_16`, `_packing`, `_packswap`, `_swap`, `_swap_alpha`, `_invert_mono`, `_invert_alpha`, `_filler`, `_add_alpha`, `_shift`, `_strip_alpha`, `_bgr`, `_interlace_handling`, `_read_user_transform_fn` |\n| 40 | `cfg40_expand_gray_to_rgb_add_alpha_swap`, `cfg40_background_gamma_strip16`, `cfg40_palette_to_rgb_expand16_bgr`, `cfg40_expand_then_quantize`, `cfg40_rgb_to_gray_background_alpha_mode`, `cfg40_strip_alpha_packing_packswap_invert_mono`, plus `cfg40_random_transform_combos` (40 000 fixed-seed random subsets of 24 transforms) |\n| 41 | `cfg41_update_info_ordering` (0×/1×/2× + `png_start_read_image`) |\n| 42 | `cfg42_progressive_read`, `cfg42_progressive_read_interlace_handling`, `cfg42_random_progressive` (1 500 random cases) |\n| 43 | `cfg43_process_data_pause_and_skip` |\n| 44 | `cfg44_progressive_combine_row` |\n| 45 | `cfg45_crc_action` (6 crit × 6 ancil × bad-IDAT/bad-tEXt), `cfg45_random_crc_corruption` (every chunk's CRC flipped in turn) |\n| 46 | `cfg46_benign_errors` (bad bKGD length, keyless tEXt, over-long sBIT, corrupt zTXt) |\n| 47 | `cfg47_user_limits`, `cfg47_random_reader_policy` (1 500 random limit/option/unknown-chunk/user-chunk policy combos) |\n| 48 | `cfg48_read_user_chunk_fn` (ret −1/0/+1) |\n| 49 | `cfg49_keep_unknown_chunks` (+ `png_handle_as_unknown`, `png_chunk_unknown_handling`) |\n| 50 | `cfg50_set_option` |\n| 51 | `cfg51_permit_mng_features` (incl. a real filter-method-64 stream) |\n| 54 | `cfg54_all_getters` |\n| 55 | `cfg55_set_rows_read_png` |\n| 56 | `cfg56_check_for_invalid_index` |\n| 64 | `cfg64_read_status_fn` |\n| 65 | `cfg65_io_state_in_read_callback` |\n| — | `fixture_sanity` — proves the synthesised inputs really contain what the rows claim (so no assertion passes vacuously) |\n| 70 | `cfg70_set_sig_bytes` |\n\nRun: `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test t_read` → **60 passed, 0 failed, 67 s**.\n\n## 2. Failing tests / divergences\n\n**None.** No C↔Rust divergence survives once the harness stops feeding the C reference undefined-behaviour inputs. Two apparent divergences were found and traced to the harness, not to the translation:\n\n- **Out-of-range background colour.** With a palette+tRNS image and `png_set_background_fixed(..., PNG_BACKGROUND_GAMMA_FILE, ...)`, `c_src/src/pngrtran.c:1712` does `back.red = png_ptr->gamma_table[png_ptr->background.red]` on a **256-entry** table. My original fuzz passed `red=4000, green=20000, blue=60000`, so C read past the table (`upd.pal0` C=0x100000 vs Rust=0xd010). Same for `need_expand=1` on ≤4-bit grey, where `pngrtran.c:1310` first multiplies the value by 0xff/0x55/0x11. Fixed by the `valid_bg()` helper, which keeps components inside the range libpng actually indexes with.\n- **`info_ptr->trans_alpha` for a colour-key tRNS.** `png_set_tRNS` sets `num_trans = 1` as a *flag* when only `trans_color` is given, leaving `trans_alpha` meaningless; after `png_set_quantize` rewrote `info->color_type` to PALETTE my snapshot started dumping it (C=208 vs Rust=0 — stale heap). Fixed by only reading `trans_alpha` when the **IHDR** colour type is PALETTE (`FILE_CT` thread-local).\n\n## 3. Not testable / caveats (all documented in the file)\n\n- **`png_process_data_pause` from the row callback livelocks the C reference.** `png_process_data_pause` zeroes `png_struct::buffer_size` while `png_push_read_IDAT` is still on the stack; on return that function does `buffer_size -= save_size`, which underflows, and `png_process_data`'s `while (buffer_size)` loop never terminates. Row 43 therefore pauses from the **info** callback (also \"within `png_process_data`\", and a safe point because the IDAT branch of `png_push_read_chunk` returns immediately after the callback). `fixture_sanity` asserts the pause really returns a non-zero byte count. `png_process_data_skip` is compared too (it is a warning + `return 0`).\n- **hIST can never be read back in 1.6.59.** The read chunk-position table gives hIST `pos_before = PNG_HAVE_PLTE` (`pngrutil.c:3065`), so a spec-conformant hIST (which must follow PLTE) is always rejected as `\"hIST: out of place\"`. The warning is compared; the quantize \"with histogram\" variants therefore supply a caller-owned histogram.\n- **`png_read_png` row padding.** `png_read_png` allocates rows with `png_malloc`, and `png_combine_row` deliberately preserves the destination bits past the last pixel (`end_mask = 0xff >> ((pixel_depth*width) & 7)`). Those bits are allocator garbage, so they are masked out before comparison.\n- **`libm` fixup.** `c_src/build/libpng.so` is linked without `-lm` (undefined `floor`, `pow`), so the test `dlopen`s `libm.so.6` with `RTLD_NOW|RTLD_GLOBAL` before touching either library. Without this the process dies with `symbol lookup error` as soon as any float path runs.\n- **Filter method 64** is only accepted when libpng has not seen a PNG signature, so the MNG stream is fed signature-stripped with `png_set_sig_bytes(pp, 8)`.\n- Only the `_fixed` variants of the gamma/background/alpha-mode/rgb-to-gray setters are exercised (as row 39 specifies); the `double` overloads are covered on the getter side (`png_get_gAMA`, `png_get_cHRM`, `png_get_sCAL`, `png_get_cLLI`). `png_get_cHRM` (double) is the one accessor missing from `tests/common/api.rs`, so it is declared in a local `decl_api!` block.\n- Rows 52/53/57–63/66–69 (memory, info-struct lifecycle, ICC internals, simplified API, low-level chunk handlers, write side) are outside this file's scope.\n\nOnly `translation/tests/t_read.rs` was created/modified (4 063 lines). Note that another agent modified `translation/src/pngread_a.rs`, `translation/src/pngstruct.rs` and `tests/common/{mod,api}.rs` at 15:47; the final run was built against that current state."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":764,"cache_read_input_tokens":319780,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":764,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Y3QfJuZCTs1j1jAHPmPmNv","session_id":"814b2895-9042-4f5f-bd73-35bea46615cb","uuid":"3b83705c-37fe-4748-a6be-46d98c1fc357","timestamp":"2026-09-08T16:20:51.193Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write t_read.rs differential tests"}
