c`, caught with `catch_unwind` — this propagates cleanly out of both C and Rust frames, so error paths are compared by *message sequence*, not just \"both failed\".\n- `c_src/build/libpng.so` is linked without `-lm` (`floor`/`pow`/`frexp` undefined). `tests/common/mod.rs` `dlopen`s `libm.so.6` with `RTLD_GLOBAL` before loading it — an environment fix, not a behaviour change.\n- Fixed three wrong prototypes (`png_write_cICP`, `png_write_iCCP`, `png_write_zTXt`), the `png_icc_check_*` signatures, and the `PNG_FREE_*` constants in the harness after sub-agents flagged them against the headers.\n- Nothing under `c_src/` was modified (only the instructed `build/` directory was added)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":305,"cache_read_input_tokens":257761,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":305,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"814b2895-9042-4f5f-bd73-35bea46615cb","uuid":"b895276e-8e1b-4604-822f-7a4419e23841","timestamp":"2026-09-08T16:28:09.608Z"}
